00:22.600 --> 00:29.430
How great is God, exalted in power, majestic above all.

00:29.500 --> 00:41.340
The heavens tell of His greatness. The skies display His awesome craftsmanship.

00:42.560 --> 00:49.260
Day after day they continue to speak. Night after night they make Him known.

00:49.330 --> 00:54.200
In creating the heavens, God also created the earth

00:54.260 --> 01:05.110
and formed man from the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life.

01:07.280 --> 01:17.130
The God of love created man and woman in His own image to have a relationship with Him.

01:17.200 --> 01:26.140
And so in the beginning, they revered and honored God and lived in harmony with Him.

01:41.740 --> 01:49.930
This continued until one day Satan tempted the woman to eat the forbidden fruit

01:50.000 --> 01:54.880
and she gave it to the man who also ate.

01:55.170 --> 02:03.510
In so doing, mankind rebelled against God and went their own way.

02:08.370 --> 02:18.310
As a result of this sin, mankind was separated from God and was thrown out of the Garden of Eden.

02:18.770 --> 02:26.700
But God still loved mankind. It was never His desire to be separate from those He created,

02:26.760 --> 02:35.400
yet how could God be holy and the source of perfect justice if He did not judge mankind for their sin?

02:35.680 --> 02:42.360
In His Holy Book, God reveals His plan to save the world from His judgment.

02:42.430 --> 02:51.110
One of the first to see this plan unfold was Abraham.

03:10.200 --> 03:19.400
Abraham was a righteous man whom God promised to bless

03:19.460 --> 03:30.940
and make his descendants as numerous as the sand of the sea and the stars of the sky.

03:39.050 --> 03:54.500
To test his obedience, God told Abraham to sacrifice his son as an offering to Him.

03:54.560 --> 04:00.710
Abraham trusted God and sought to obey Him.

04:15.800 --> 04:25.830
But as he raised his knife to kill his son, the angel of the Lord stopped Him.

04:25.900 --> 04:31.800
He saw that Abraham feared God and was willing to obey Him.

04:32.370 --> 04:37.750
Then Abraham saw a ram caught by its horns in a thicket,

04:37.910 --> 04:44.540
and he sacrificed the ram instead of his son as an offering to God.

04:44.880 --> 04:53.430
And so God showed Abraham that a lamb or a similar animal was to be slain as a temporary covering for sin

04:53.500 --> 05:00.320
until God would provide His ultimate sacrifice to pay for the sins of mankind.

05:00.390 --> 05:08.880
Instead of sin separating man from God, the sacrifice would restore their relationship.

05:09.680 --> 05:17.560
The Holy Scriptures speak of One who was to come and be the ultimate sacrifice for the sins of the world.

05:17.630 --> 05:20.630
As the ram took the place of Abraham's son,

05:20.700 --> 05:26.760
so this One who would come would take man's place so he could be forgiven.

05:26.830 --> 05:29.360
Some refer to this person as the Messiah,

05:29.430 --> 05:38.940
the One who would come and reconcile the world back to God once and for all.

06:01.800 --> 06:15.800
The prophets predicted many things in detail about the Messiah hundreds of years before He appeared.

06:16.480 --> 06:23.000
The prophet Isaiah foretold that His birth was to be a miraculous one.

06:23.060 --> 06:30.060
A virgin would conceive a child who was to be called, the Son of God.

06:30.130 --> 06:35.330
The prophet Micah predicted that the Messiah would be born in Bethlehem,

06:35.400 --> 06:40.960
while the prophet Zechariah foretold His entry into Jerusalem on a donkey

06:41.030 --> 06:46.140
and His betrayal by Judas, one of His followers.

06:46.880 --> 06:53.000
Isaiah prophesied what the Messiah would do when He came.

06:53.060 --> 06:59.440
The Lord's anointed will preach the Good News to the poor, bind up the brokenhearted,

06:59.480 --> 07:08.880
proclaim freedom for the captives and proclaim that the time has come when the Lord will save His people.

07:10.080 --> 07:19.100
So, who was the Messiah? In the first century, a prophet came called Jesus.

07:19.160 --> 07:24.700
Some thought He was the one the prophet spoke about. Could this be?

07:24.760 --> 07:31.860
Did His life fulfill what was predicted of Him? Was Jesus more than a prophet?

07:31.930 --> 07:41.970
What follows is His story, based on eyewitness accounts as recorded in The Holy Scriptures.

07:42.600 --> 07:48.460
An actor plays the part of Jesus, and though no actor is worthy of such a role,

07:48.530 --> 07:55.620
it has been done so that we may understand and benefit from the life of Jesus.

08:01.670 --> 08:07.060
<b>I am writing to you, dear Theophilus, an orderly account of the things that have taken place among us,</b>

08:07.130 --> 08:12.070
<b>so that you may know the absolute truth about everything.</b>

08:18.990 --> 08:24.880
<b>In the days when Caesar Augustus was emperor of Rome, and when Herod the Great was king of Judea,</b>

08:24.930 --> 08:32.720
<b>God sent the angel Gabriel to visit a virgin of the city of Nazareth. And the virgin's name was Mary.</b>

08:45.420 --> 08:50.410
<b>Fear not Mary, for you have found favor with God.</b>

08:50.480 --> 08:57.100
<b>You will conceive and give birth to a Son and you will call His name "Jesus."</b>

08:57.200 --> 08:58.730
<b>How can this be?</b>

08:58.800 --> 09:00.030
<b>I am a virgin.</b>

09:00.150 --> 09:02.300
<b>The Holy Spirit will come upon you.</b>

09:02.380 --> 09:11.260
<b>For this reason the Holy Child will be called the Son of the Most High God. His kingdom will never end.</b>

09:11.410 --> 09:15.250
<b>Mary went to visit her cousin Elizabeth, who was too old to have a child.</b>

09:15.320 --> 09:17.760
<b>But by a miracle, God enabled her to become pregnant.</b>

09:17.780 --> 09:19.030
<b>Elizabeth!</b>

09:19.080 --> 09:20.220
<b>Mary!</b>

09:20.480 --> 09:23.000
<b>Cousin Mary!</b>

09:24.580 --> 09:27.320
<b>You are the most blessed of all women,</b>

09:27.470 --> 09:30.180
<b>and blessed is the Child you will bear.</b>

09:30.280 --> 09:32.430
<b>For as soon as I heard your greeting,</b>

09:32.600 --> 09:34.300
<b>the baby within me</b>

09:34.380 --> 09:36.200
<b>jumped with gladness.</b>

09:36.270 --> 09:39.600
<b>My soul magnifies the Lord,</b>

09:39.970 --> 09:43.670
<b>And my spirit has rejoiced in God my Savior.</b>

09:44.070 --> 09:47.580
<b>From now on all generations will call me blessed.</b>

09:54.180 --> 09:59.930
<b>Know, all men of Nazareth, that by command of Caesar Augustus,</b>

10:00.000 --> 10:06.600
<b>there will be conducted a census of the subject territories of Galilee and Judea.</b>

10:06.630 --> 10:14.550
<b>All men must register in the town or city where their ancestors were born.</b>

10:18.300 --> 10:25.190
<b>So Joseph went to the town of Bethlehem in Judea to register with Mary, to whom he was engaged.</b>

10:30.020 --> 10:37.590
<b>But there was no room for them in Bethlehem. And the only lodging they could find was a humble stable.</b>

10:48.670 --> 10:53.400
<b>Now there were some shepherds in that part of the country who were taking care of their flock at night.</b>

10:53.480 --> 10:59.550
<b>Suddenly, an angel of God appeared to them and the glory of God shone about them.</b>

11:03.620 --> 11:11.930
<b>This very day in David's town your Savior was born.  He is Christ the Lord.</b>

11:17.570 --> 11:21.620
<b>The shepherds hurried to see the newborn Babe in the manger,</b>

11:21.720 --> 11:28.600
<b>and were the first to spread the Good News or "Gospel" of the  the Savior's birth.</b>

11:36.220 --> 11:42.280
<b>A week later, when the time came for the Baby to be circumcised, He was given the name Jesus,</b>

11:42.330 --> 11:46.580
<b>and Joseph and Mary took the Child to Jerusalem to present Him to the Lord.</b>

11:46.650 --> 11:51.440
<b>In the temple there was a good and devout man named Simeon.</b>

11:51.490 --> 11:55.090
<b>The Holy Spirit had promised him that he would not die until he had seen the Christ.</b>

11:55.200 --> 12:00.900
<b>Lord, now let Your servant depart in peace according to Your promise.</b>

12:06.600 --> 12:10.380
<b>For my eyes have seen Your salvation.</b>

12:10.580 --> 12:13.270
<b>This Child is chosen by God.</b>

12:14.050 --> 12:17.550
<b>May you both be blessed.</b>

12:24.030 --> 12:27.800
<b>They completed their duties according to the religious law.</b>

12:27.880 --> 12:34.430
<b>Then, some time later, they returned to their home in Nazareth.</b>

12:34.780 --> 12:41.300
<b>When Jesus was twelve years old, Joseph and Mary took Him to Jerusalem for the passover feast.</b>

12:41.390 --> 12:51.640
<b>But when they started back home, thinking that the Boy was with them, Jesus stayed behind.</b>

12:51.960 --> 12:54.840
<b>They returned to the city to look for Him,</b>

12:54.920 --> 12:59.800
<b>and three days later they found Him in the temple sitting with the Jewish religious teachers.</b>

13:00.140 --> 13:03.320
<b>Whose Child is this who asks such questions?</b>

13:03.360 --> 13:04.620
<b>He's from Nazareth.</b>

13:04.800 --> 13:06.500
<b>We thought He had left with us.</b>

13:06.570 --> 13:08.380
<b>Please, forgive Him his zeal.</b>

13:08.440 --> 13:11.580
<b>All who heard Him were amazed.</b>

13:16.090 --> 13:22.590
<b>Son, why have You done this to us? Your father and I have been terribly worried trying to find You.</b>

13:23.090 --> 13:28.600
<b>Why were you looking for me?  Didn't you know that I must do the work of my Father?</b>

13:33.900 --> 13:42.910
<b>And He came with them to Nazareth and increased in wisdom and stature and in favor with God and with man.</b>

13:44.510 --> 13:50.620
<b>This is the true story of the life of Jesus.</b>

13:51.620 --> 13:57.730
<b>It is taken from the Gospel of Luke.</b>

13:58.760 --> 14:04.880
<b>Inspirational Films, Inc. Presents</b>

14:05.880 --> 14:12.010
<b>JESUS</b>

14:13.740 --> 14:17.230
<b>In the fifteenth year of the rule of the emperor Tiberius,</b>

14:17.300 --> 14:20.160
<b>when Pontius Pilate was governor of Judea,</b>

14:20.280 --> 14:23.050
<b>and Herod was the ruler of Galilee,</b>

14:23.420 --> 14:27.260
<b>and Annas and Caiaphas were the high priests.</b>

14:27.620 --> 14:33.390
<b>The word of God came to John, the son of Elizabeth, and he went through all the country along the Jordan River,</b>

14:33.470 --> 14:36.760
<b>preaching the baptism of repentance for the remission of sins.</b>

14:36.800 --> 14:39.340
<b>Turn away from your sins</b>

14:39.540 --> 14:41.370
<b>and be baptized,</b>

14:41.470 --> 14:44.530
<b>and God will forgive your sins!</b>

14:45.020 --> 14:51.280
<b>As it is written in the book of the prophet Isaiah:</b>

14:51.440 --> 14:55.890
<b>"Someone is shouting in the desert:</b>

14:55.960 --> 15:00.170
<b>Get the road ready for the Lord!'</b>

15:00.350 --> 15:03.950
<b>Make a straight path for Him to travel.</b>

15:04.100 --> 15:07.880
<b>Every valley must be filled up;</b>

15:08.010 --> 15:11.600
<b>every hill and mountain leveled off!</b>

15:12.030 --> 15:19.980
<b>The winding roads must be made straight, and the rough paths made smooth.</b>

15:20.100 --> 15:23.480
<b>And all mankind</b>

15:23.610 --> 15:25.780
<b>will see God's salvation!'"</b>

15:25.780 --> 15:27.040
<b>What shall we do?</b>

15:27.100 --> 15:28.290
<b>Yes, tell us, what must we do?</b>

15:28.370 --> 15:30.370
<b>You brood of vipers!</b>

15:30.430 --> 15:32.590
<b>What do you want us to do?</b>

15:34.160 --> 15:37.920
<b>Help us. Tell us which way to turn.</b>

15:37.980 --> 15:40.600
<b>Whoever has two</b>

15:40.770 --> 15:42.500
<b>shirts,</b>

15:42.710 --> 15:45.700
<b>must give one to the man</b>

15:45.870 --> 15:46.900
<b>who has</b>

15:46.970 --> 15:48.200
<b>none.</b>

15:49.340 --> 15:51.040
<b>And whoever has food</b>

15:51.410 --> 15:52.540
<b>must share it.</b>

15:54.300 --> 15:55.940
<b>Teacher,</b>

15:59.380 --> 16:02.320
<b>we are tax collectors.</b>

16:02.630 --> 16:03.750
<b>What shall we do?</b>

16:05.450 --> 16:08.150
<b>Don't collect more than is legal.</b>

16:08.210 --> 16:09.730
<b>And what about us?</b>

16:10.080 --> 16:11.550
<b>What are we to do?</b>

16:11.670 --> 16:14.930
<b>Don't take money from anyone by force.</b>

16:15.170 --> 16:18.540
<b>And don't accuse anyone falsely.</b>

16:18.740 --> 16:21.850
<b>Be content with your pay.</b>

16:31.300 --> 16:32.250
<b>Tell us...</b>

16:32.580 --> 16:33.650
<b>are you</b>

16:33.680 --> 16:34.880
<b>the Christ?</b>

16:40.510 --> 16:43.690
<b>I baptize you with water.</b>

16:44.050 --> 16:48.360
<b>But Someone is coming who is much greater than I am.</b>

16:48.530 --> 16:56.270
<b>I'm not good enough even to untie His sandals. He will baptize you with the Holy Spirit and fire.</b>

16:56.320 --> 17:05.580
<b>He has His threshing fork with Him, to thresh out all the grain and gather the wheat into His barn.</b>

17:33.010 --> 17:41.920
<b>And God the Holy Spirit came down upon Jesus in bodily form like a dove.</b>

17:43.990 --> 17:53.550
<b>And a voice from heaven said, "You are My beloved Son, in You I am well pleased".</b>

17:58.560 --> 18:05.340
<b>When Jesus began His work He was about thirty years old. He returned from the Jordan full of the Holy Spirit</b>

18:05.440 --> 18:11.200
<b>and was led by the Spirit into the desert where He was tempted by the devil for forty days.</b>

18:11.240 --> 18:14.630
<b>In all this time He ate nothing.</b>

18:36.150 --> 18:38.560
<b>And the devil said to Him:</b>

18:38.560 --> 18:43.110
<b>If you are God's Son, order this stone to turn into bread.</b>

18:48.480 --> 18:49.890
<b>It is written</b>

18:50.240 --> 18:53.580
<b>that man shall not live by bread alone but by every word of God.</b>

19:06.900 --> 19:11.540
<b>Then the devil took Him up and showed Him in a moment all the kingdoms of the world.</b>

19:12.710 --> 19:16.880
<b>I will give You all this power and all this wealth.</b>

19:16.930 --> 19:21.880
<b>It has all been handed over to me and I can give it to anyone I choose.</b>

19:21.930 --> 19:25.970
<b>All this will be Yours then, if You worship me.</b>

19:26.420 --> 19:29.460
<b>It is written, "You shall worship the Lord your God,</b>

19:29.820 --> 19:31.550
<b>and Him only shall you serve."</b>

19:38.900 --> 19:43.560
<b>Then the devil took Him to Jerusalem and set Him on the highest point of the temple.</b>

19:43.640 --> 19:47.300
<b>If you are God's Son, throw Yourself down from here,</b>

19:47.380 --> 19:51.560
<b>for the Scripture says: "God will order His angels to take good care of You."</b>

19:51.650 --> 19:58.170
<b>They "will hold You up with their hands, so that not even Your feet will be hurt on the stones."</b>

19:58.190 --> 20:00.350
<b>The Scripture says,</b>

20:00.690 --> 20:03.570
<b>"You shall not put the Lord your God to the test."</b>

20:28.180 --> 20:31.580
<b>And He came to Nazareth where He had been brought up.</b>

20:51.010 --> 20:51.810
<b>Hello.</b>

20:51.860 --> 20:53.040
<b>Hello.</b>

21:00.070 --> 21:05.310
<b>And on the Sabbath He went as usual to the synagogue.</b>

21:14.320 --> 21:19.560
<b>And He was called upon to read a portion of the Prophet Isaiah.</b>

21:46.850 --> 21:49.470
<b>"The Spirit of the Lord is upon Me,</b>

21:49.820 --> 21:52.840
<b>because He has chosen Me to bring good news to the poor.</b>

21:53.340 --> 21:58.080
<b>He has sent Me to proclaim release to the captives and recovery of sight to the blind.</b>

21:58.240 --> 22:00.970
<b>To set at liberty those who are oppressed,</b>

22:01.180 --> 22:04.990
<b>and announce that the time has come when the Lord will save His people."</b>

22:05.180 --> 22:08.560
<b>He speaks well.</b>

22:18.380 --> 22:20.700
<b>This passage of Scripture has come true today,</b>

22:20.760 --> 22:22.090
<b>as you heard it being read.</b>

22:22.200 --> 22:23.630
<b>The Scripture come true?</b>

22:23.900 --> 22:26.030
<b>But only the Messiah can fulfill that promise!</b>

22:26.100 --> 22:27.540
<b>How shall we know?</b>

22:28.270 --> 22:30.440
<b>Doubtless you will quote the proverb to Me,</b>

22:30.510 --> 22:32.510
<b>"Physician heal yourself."</b>

22:32.650 --> 22:34.060
<b>You'll also say to Me,</b>

22:34.100 --> 22:36.150
<b>"Now do the things in Your own home town,</b>

22:36.210 --> 22:38.040
<b>that we heard You did in Capernaum."</b>

22:38.180 --> 22:39.460
<b>I tell you this,</b>

22:39.540 --> 22:42.550
<b>no prophet is ever welcome in his hometown!</b>

22:43.080 --> 22:49.700
<b>By these words Jesus identified Himself as the Messiah, God's Anointed, sent to save His people.</b>

22:49.730 --> 22:54.700
<b>These Jews did not accept Him as the Messiah.</b>

22:54.890 --> 22:57.010
<b>They meant to throw Him over the cliff,</b>

22:57.100 --> 23:00.530
<b>but He walked through the middle of the crowd,</b>

23:00.650 --> 23:03.490
<b>and went His way,</b>

23:09.800 --> 23:14.570
<b>and came to Capernaum, a city of Galilee.</b>

23:17.770 --> 23:22.060
<b>The Roman occupation in the nation was in evidence everywhere.</b>

23:22.110 --> 23:27.600
<b>And the people longed for the Messiah, to free them from the tyranny.</b>

23:50.150 --> 23:51.080
<b>Peace be with you.</b>

23:51.110 --> 23:52.580
<b>And you, Master.</b>

23:52.920 --> 23:54.720
<b>May I use your boat, Simon?</b>

23:55.490 --> 23:56.580
<b>Why not?</b>

24:00.020 --> 24:01.930
<b>He's not going to leave is He?</b>

24:02.460 --> 24:04.520
<b>Speak to us! Speak to us!</b>

24:04.580 --> 24:05.430
<b>Speak to us!</b>

24:05.560 --> 24:07.530
<b>Jesus, speak to us!</b>

24:18.710 --> 24:22.310
<b>Once there were two men who went up to the temple to pray.</b>

24:22.690 --> 24:26.050
<b>One was a Pharisee, the other a tax collector.</b>

24:26.420 --> 24:29.630
<b>The Pharisee stood apart by himself and prayed,</b>

24:29.960 --> 24:35.420
<b>"I thank you God that I am not greedy or dishonest or an adulterer like everybody else.</b>

24:35.490 --> 24:39.580
<b>I thank you that I am not like that tax collector over there."</b>

24:40.400 --> 24:42.470
<b>"I fast twice a week,</b>

24:42.830 --> 24:45.360
<b>and I give you one tenth of all my income."</b>

24:45.530 --> 24:50.010
<b>But the tax collector stood at a distance and would not even raise his face to heaven,</b>

24:50.100 --> 24:52.180
<b>but beat upon his breast and said,</b>

24:52.280 --> 24:54.840
<b>"God, have pity on me, a sinner."</b>

24:55.810 --> 25:02.190
<b>I tell you, the tax collector, not the Pharisee, was in the right with God when he went home.</b>

25:02.550 --> 25:05.950
<b>For the man who exalts himself will be humbled,</b>

25:06.320 --> 25:07.920
<b>and he who humbles himself</b>

25:08.160 --> 25:09.590
<b>will be exalted.</b>

25:11.970 --> 25:14.670
<b>Push the boat out farther to the deep water.</b>

25:14.990 --> 25:17.560
<b>Then you and your partners let down your nets for a catch.</b>

25:17.670 --> 25:19.210
<b>Oh, Master,</b>

25:19.240 --> 25:21.480
<b>we worked hard all night long</b>

25:21.830 --> 25:23.890
<b>and caught nothing.</b>

25:27.930 --> 25:29.990
<b>But if You say so,</b>

25:30.310 --> 25:32.390
<b>I'll let down the nets.</b>

25:33.350 --> 25:34.390
<b>James!</b>

25:34.680 --> 25:35.770
<b>John!</b>

25:51.500 --> 25:59.100
<b>(laughing)</b>

25:59.480 --> 26:03.060
<b>James! John! Get your boat over here and give us some help! Hurry!</b>

26:03.150 --> 26:05.360
<b>We can't, we've got our hands full.</b>

26:13.290 --> 26:18.560
<b>[laughing]</b>

26:43.460 --> 26:46.250
<b>Go away from me, Lord.</b>

26:46.590 --> 26:48.590
<b>I am a sinful man.</b>

26:48.630 --> 26:50.160
<b>Don't be afraid.</b>

26:50.540 --> 26:52.820
<b>From now on you will be catching men.</b>

27:04.530 --> 27:11.330
<b>Come to Me and listen to My words. Hear Me, and you shall have life.</b>

27:11.490 --> 27:17.250
<b>Seek the Lord while He may be found; call on Him while He is near.</b>

27:17.420 --> 27:22.250
<b>Let the wicked forsake his way, and the unrighteous man his thoughts;</b>

27:22.440 --> 27:25.740
<b>and let him return to the Lord and He will have compassion on him.</b>

27:25.860 --> 27:31.480
<b>For He will abundantly pardon. You shall go out with joy and be led forth in peace.</b>

27:31.990 --> 27:35.640
<b>He's coming! He's here! Look!</b>

27:35.700 --> 27:37.920
<b>Jesus! Jesus!</b>

27:38.020 --> 27:40.010
<b>I beg you to save my only daughter!</b>

27:40.270 --> 27:45.990
<b>Sir, have mercy. She's only twelve years old and... and dying. Please! Please, come with me!</b>

27:46.190 --> 27:48.100
<b>Jairus, I'm sorry.</b>

27:48.450 --> 27:49.460
<b>Jesus!</b>

27:49.490 --> 27:50.820
<b>Your daughter has died.</b>

27:50.890 --> 27:52.740
<b>Don't bother the teacher any longer.</b>

27:52.850 --> 27:54.550
<b>Don't be afraid.</b>

27:54.930 --> 27:57.110
<b>Only believe, and she will be well.</b>

28:52.100 --> 28:54.190
<b>Do not weep.</b>

28:54.510 --> 28:57.980
<b>She's not dead, but only sleeping.</b>

29:05.910 --> 29:08.140
<b>Child,</b>

29:08.490 --> 29:10.180
<b>arise.</b>

29:32.800 --> 29:34.550
<b>Give her something to eat.</b>

29:35.480 --> 29:37.060
<b>Listen to me,</b>

29:37.270 --> 29:39.560
<b>tell no one what has happened here.</b>

29:45.060 --> 29:52.570
<b>And after this he saw a publican named Matthew Levi, sitting at the toll gate for the receipt of the customs.</b>

30:12.140 --> 30:13.520
<b>Follow Me.</b>

30:53.880 --> 31:00.530
<b>And Jesus went up a hill to pray, and spent the whole night there praying to God.</b>

31:13.130 --> 31:19.560
<b>And when day came He greeted the twelve of them whom He named apostles.</b>

31:23.800 --> 31:30.250
<b>Simon, whom He also named Peter...</b>

31:31.380 --> 31:36.410
<b>and Andrew, his brother...</b>

31:37.030 --> 31:43.000
<b>James...</b>

31:44.050 --> 31:49.550
<b>and John...</b>

31:49.860 --> 31:54.720
<b>Philip...</b>

31:55.160 --> 31:59.500
<b>and Bartholomew...</b>

31:59.580 --> 32:06.770
<b>and Matthew...</b>

32:07.830 --> 32:11.830
<b>and Thomas...</b>

32:12.160 --> 32:17.780
<b>James, the son of Alphaeus...</b>

32:18.510 --> 32:22.920
<b>and Simon called Zealotes...</b>

32:23.390 --> 32:27.240
<b>and Judas, the brother of James...</b>

32:28.920 --> 32:34.030
<b>and Judas Iscariot, the one who would later betray Jesus.</b>

33:05.920 --> 33:07.760
<b>Blessed are you poor,</b>

33:07.940 --> 33:10.070
<b>for yours is the kingdom of God.</b>

33:10.260 --> 33:13.150
<b>Blessed are you who hunger now, for you shall be filled.</b>

33:13.320 --> 33:16.210
<b>Blessed are you who weep now, for you shall laugh.</b>

33:16.490 --> 33:22.660
<b>Blessed are you when men hate you and reject you and insult you, and say you are evil, all because of the Son of Man.</b>

33:22.920 --> 33:27.970
<b>Be glad when that happens and dance for joy, because a great reward is kept for you in heaven.</b>

33:28.160 --> 33:31.450
<b>For their ancestors did the very same thing to the prophets.</b>

33:36.760 --> 33:43.420
<b>...seventeen, eighteen, nineteen, That's all I've got.</b>

33:43.470 --> 33:44.490
<b>What do you mean that's all you've got!</b>

33:44.540 --> 33:46.980
<b>How terrible for you who are rich now!</b>

33:47.310 --> 33:49.070
<b>You have had your easy life.</b>

33:51.580 --> 33:56.990
<b>(Laughing)</b>

33:57.320 --> 34:00.540
<b>He doesn't want to be rich.  He must be mad.</b>

34:01.280 --> 34:03.430
<b>How terrible for you who laugh now,</b>

34:03.780 --> 34:05.510
<b>for you shall mourn and weep.</b>

34:09.130 --> 34:12.130
<b>How terrible when all men speak well of you,</b>

34:12.500 --> 34:17.110
<b>for their ancestors said the very same things about the false prophets.</b>

34:18.770 --> 34:20.710
<b>But I tell you who hear Me:</b>

34:21.110 --> 34:22.860
<b>Love your enemies.</b>

34:24.210 --> 34:27.010
<b>Do good to those who hate you.</b>

34:27.360 --> 34:30.420
<b>Bless those who curse you.</b>

34:30.750 --> 34:33.690
<b>And pray for those who mistreat you.</b>

34:40.630 --> 34:43.840
<b>If anyone strikes you on the one cheek,</b>

34:44.210 --> 34:46.840
<b>let him hit the other one also.</b>

34:52.540 --> 34:58.230
<b>And if someone takes away your coat, let him have your shirt as well.</b>

34:58.590 --> 35:01.590
<b>Give to everyone who asks you for something.</b>

35:03.630 --> 35:05.690
<b>And if someone takes what is yours,</b>

35:06.050 --> 35:08.210
<b>do not ask for it back again.</b>

35:11.920 --> 35:13.480
<b>Do for others</b>

35:13.730 --> 35:16.150
<b>only what you would have others do for you.</b>

35:21.860 --> 35:25.270
<b>If you love only the people who love you,</b>

35:25.650 --> 35:28.570
<b>why should you receive a blessing?</b>

35:28.790 --> 35:31.090
<b>For even sinners love those who love them.</b>

35:31.230 --> 35:34.380
<b>And if you do good to those who do good to you,</b>

35:34.610 --> 35:37.130
<b>why should you receive a blessing?</b>

35:38.150 --> 35:40.250
<b>Even sinners do that.</b>

35:40.320 --> 35:41.840
<b>How could He touch her?</b>

35:41.960 --> 35:43.520
<b>How could He talk to her?</b>

35:44.960 --> 35:46.530
<b>Disgusting!</b>

35:53.860 --> 35:55.630
<b>No,</b>

35:55.790 --> 35:57.710
<b>love your enemies,</b>

35:57.780 --> 35:59.110
<b>and do good to them.</b>

35:59.270 --> 36:01.820
<b>And lend expecting nothing back.</b>

36:01.960 --> 36:04.320
<b>And then you will have a great reward,</b>

36:04.510 --> 36:08.010
<b>for you will be sons of the Most High God.</b>

36:08.230 --> 36:11.520
<b>For He is good to the ungrateful and to the wicked.</b>

36:11.670 --> 36:13.210
<b>Be merciful,</b>

36:13.420 --> 36:16.020
<b>just as your Father is merciful.</b>

36:20.170 --> 36:21.570
<b>Save us, Jesus!</b>

36:22.320 --> 36:25.840
<b>Judge not and you will not be judged!</b>

36:26.010 --> 36:27.530
<b>Condemn not,</b>

36:27.610 --> 36:30.650
<b>and you will not be condemned!</b>

36:30.770 --> 36:32.670
<b>Forgive,</b>

36:32.880 --> 36:34.420
<b>and you will be forgiven.</b>

36:34.610 --> 36:36.860
<b>Lead us in Your path, Lord!</b>

36:41.960 --> 36:45.460
<b>Give, and it will be given to you.</b>

36:45.630 --> 36:48.980
<b>For the measure you give will be the measure you get back.</b>

36:51.040 --> 36:54.090
<b>One blind man cannot lead another!</b>

36:54.260 --> 36:57.760
<b>If he does they will both fall into a ditch.</b>

36:57.900 --> 37:02.920
<b>Why do you see the speck that is in your brother's eye but pay no attention to the log in your own eye?</b>

37:06.960 --> 37:08.960
<b>Guide us, Master!</b>

37:09.070 --> 37:10.880
<b>We need You now, Lord!</b>

37:11.010 --> 37:14.010
<b>How happy is the mother who bore You and nursed You!</b>

37:14.010 --> 37:14.590
<b>(Laughing)</b>

37:14.710 --> 37:17.230
<b>Rather how happy are those who hear the word of God,</b>

37:17.320 --> 37:18.940
<b>and obey it.</b>

37:22.230 --> 37:24.520
<b>I would like to know this Man.</b>

37:25.190 --> 37:27.190
<b>Do you think He might be</b>

37:27.380 --> 37:29.530
<b>the Messiah?</b>

37:36.230 --> 37:43.500
<b>This pharisee invited Jesus to have dinner with him.  And Jesus went to his house and sat down to eat.</b>

37:45.230 --> 37:47.250
<b>Come along children, off you go.</b>

37:47.610 --> 37:48.610
<b>You heard me,</b>

37:48.650 --> 37:49.730
<b>go!</b>

37:49.860 --> 37:53.420
<b>They get into all the mischief they can, but they're good sons.</b>

37:56.070 --> 37:57.820
<b>What is she doing here?</b>

37:57.860 --> 37:59.070
<b>I don't know.</b>

38:17.880 --> 38:21.090
<b>What is she doing?</b>

38:31.760 --> 38:37.940
<b>If this Man really were a prophet He would know who this woman is who is touching Him.</b>

38:41.270 --> 38:44.070
<b>He would know what kind of a sinful life she lives.</b>

38:44.400 --> 38:47.270
<b>I know who this woman is, Simon.</b>

38:47.460 --> 38:49.070
<b>Let Me tell you something.</b>

38:49.250 --> 38:52.090
<b>There were two men who owed money to a money lender.</b>

38:52.340 --> 38:55.190
<b>One owed him 500 silver coins and the other 50.</b>

38:55.360 --> 38:57.480
<b>Neither of them could pay him back, so he</b>

38:57.590 --> 38:59.630
<b>canceled the debts of both.</b>

38:59.820 --> 39:02.090
<b>Which one then will love him more?</b>

39:02.190 --> 39:04.900
<b>I suppose that it would be the one who was forgiven more.</b>

39:04.960 --> 39:07.480
<b>You are right.</b>

39:07.860 --> 39:10.070
<b>You see this woman?</b>

39:10.840 --> 39:15.420
<b>I came into your home. You gave Me no water for My feet,</b>

39:15.480 --> 39:19.460
<b>yet she has washed My feet with her tears and dried them with her hair.</b>

39:19.980 --> 39:22.710
<b>You did not welcome Me with a kiss,</b>

39:22.860 --> 39:26.420
<b>but since I came she has not stopped kissing My feet.</b>

39:26.630 --> 39:29.710
<b>You provided no olive oil for My head,</b>

39:29.900 --> 39:33.820
<b>yet she has anointed My feet with perfume.</b>

39:34.010 --> 39:35.960
<b>I tell you then,</b>

39:36.130 --> 39:40.340
<b>the great love she has shown proves that her many sins are forgiven.</b>

39:40.500 --> 39:42.340
<b>But whoever is forgiven little,</b>

39:42.480 --> 39:45.070
<b>shows only a little love.</b>

39:57.480 --> 39:59.650
<b>Your sins are forgiven you.</b>

39:59.800 --> 40:02.480
<b>How can He say that?  How can He forgive sins?  He speaks blasphemy!</b>

40:02.530 --> 40:05.420
<b>Your faith has saved you.  Go in peace.</b>

40:31.940 --> 40:36.020
<b>And Jesus traveled about, teaching the good news of the kingdom of God.</b>

40:36.070 --> 40:41.800
<b>And the twelve disciples went with Him and so did some women who had been healed of evil spirits:</b>

40:42.230 --> 40:44.880
<b>Mary, who was called Magdalene,</b>

40:45.380 --> 40:50.630
<b>Joanna, whose husband, Chuza, was steward in Herod's court,</b>

40:50.790 --> 40:53.030
<b>and Susanna.</b>

41:04.750 --> 41:10.510
<b>But Herod, the Roman appointed ruler of Galilee, threw John the Baptist in prison,</b>

41:10.610 --> 41:15.070
<b>because he had condemned his marriage to his brother's wife.</b>

41:16.030 --> 41:16.900
<b>Well?</b>

41:16.920 --> 41:19.020
<b>As we arrived at the gate of Nain,</b>

41:19.190 --> 41:21.300
<b>a funeral procession came out.</b>

41:21.420 --> 41:23.840
<b>The dead was the only son of a widow.</b>

41:23.920 --> 41:30.090
<b>When Jesus saw her, His heart was filled with compassion. He touched the coffin and said,</b>

41:30.150 --> 41:32.320
<b>"Young man, get up I tell you."</b>

41:32.460 --> 41:37.170
<b>Then the dead man sat up, and Jesus gave him back to his mother.</b>

41:37.290 --> 41:38.230
<b>Ask Him,</b>

41:38.380 --> 41:39.440
<b>say,</b>

41:39.670 --> 41:43.550
<b>"Are You the One John said was going to come,</b>

41:43.690 --> 41:47.090
<b>or should we expect someone else?"</b>

42:16.210 --> 42:17.590
<b>Master!</b>

42:25.800 --> 42:27.030
<b>Master!</b>

42:28.050 --> 42:30.570
<b>John the Baptist sent us to ask</b>

42:30.670 --> 42:32.840
<b>if You are the One who is going to come,</b>

42:32.940 --> 42:35.030
<b>or should we expect someone else?</b>

42:35.170 --> 42:37.840
<b>Go back and tell John what you have seen and heard:</b>

42:38.210 --> 42:39.530
<b>the blind can see,</b>

42:39.670 --> 42:41.440
<b>the lame can walk.</b>

42:41.650 --> 42:44.380
<b>How happy are those who have no doubts about Me.</b>

42:52.780 --> 42:54.860
<b>Please, pick me up.</b>

42:55.260 --> 42:58.150
<b>Onto my shoulder. Can you see now?</b>

42:58.230 --> 43:00.400
<b>I can see Jesus.</b>

43:03.070 --> 43:06.210
<b>A sower went out to sow his seed.</b>

43:06.420 --> 43:10.650
<b>And as he scattered the grain, some of it fell by the path and was walked upon,</b>

43:10.840 --> 43:13.170
<b>and the birds of the air devoured it.</b>

43:14.960 --> 43:17.440
<b>And some fell on rocky ground,</b>

43:17.570 --> 43:21.710
<b>and when the plants sprouted, they withered away because they had no moisture.</b>

43:22.570 --> 43:25.730
<b>And some seeds fell among thorns,</b>

43:25.920 --> 43:28.260
<b>and the thorns grew up with the plants</b>

43:28.440 --> 43:29.840
<b>and choked them.</b>

43:30.690 --> 43:33.860
<b>And some seeds fell in good soil,</b>

43:33.960 --> 43:37.110
<b>and the plants grew and bore grain,</b>

43:37.300 --> 43:39.280
<b>100 grains each.</b>

43:39.840 --> 43:41.070
<b>Master,</b>

43:41.320 --> 43:44.440
<b>why do You speak in parables whenever a crowd is near?</b>

43:44.530 --> 43:48.210
<b>The knowledge of the secrets of the kingdom of God has been given to you.</b>

43:48.460 --> 43:52.920
<b>But to others I speak in parables, so that they may look but not see,</b>

43:53.070 --> 43:55.090
<b>and listen but not understand.</b>

44:03.440 --> 44:06.550
<b>This is what the parable means.</b>

44:14.920 --> 44:18.440
<b>The seed is the Word of God.</b>

44:20.690 --> 44:24.210
<b>The seeds that fell along the path stand for those who hear.</b>

44:24.380 --> 44:30.510
<b>But the devil comes, and takes the message away from their hearts in order to keep them from believing and being saved.</b>

44:30.980 --> 44:36.420
<b>The seeds that fell on rocky ground stand for those who hear the message and receive it gladly,</b>

44:36.690 --> 44:38.420
<b>but they have no roots.</b>

44:38.650 --> 44:40.630
<b>They believe only for a while.</b>

44:40.820 --> 44:42.960
<b>And when the time of testing comes,</b>

44:43.340 --> 44:44.590
<b>they fall away.</b>

44:45.590 --> 44:49.630
<b>The seeds that fell among thorns stand for those who hear,</b>

44:49.800 --> 44:55.150
<b>but the worries and riches and pleasures of this life crowd in and choke them</b>

44:55.340 --> 44:58.090
<b>and their fruit never ripens.</b>

44:59.480 --> 45:02.190
<b>And the seeds that fell in good soil</b>

45:02.440 --> 45:06.860
<b>stand for those who hear the message and retain it in a good and obedient heart,</b>

45:07.070 --> 45:10.090
<b>and they persist until they bear fruit.</b>

45:17.340 --> 45:20.050
<b>No one lights a lamp and covers it with a bowl,</b>

45:20.230 --> 45:21.980
<b>or puts it under a bed.</b>

45:22.130 --> 45:24.320
<b>Instead he puts it on the stand,</b>

45:24.400 --> 45:27.340
<b>so that the people may see the light as they come in.</b>

45:27.860 --> 45:30.840
<b>Whatever is hidden away will be brought out in the open...</b>

45:30.900 --> 45:34.380
<b>And whatever is covered up will be found and brought to light.</b>

45:35.210 --> 45:37.590
<b>Be careful then how you listen,</b>

45:37.760 --> 45:40.820
<b>because whoever has will be given more,</b>

45:41.010 --> 45:45.190
<b>but he who has not will have taken away from him even the little he thinks he has.</b>

45:45.320 --> 45:46.050
<b>Teacher,</b>

45:46.260 --> 45:48.400
<b>your mother and brothers are standing outside.</b>

45:48.510 --> 45:49.710
<b>They want to see You.</b>

45:49.880 --> 45:52.760
<b>My mother and brothers are those who hear the Word of God,</b>

45:52.900 --> 45:54.260
<b>and obey it.</b>

46:02.710 --> 46:11.010
<b>One day Jesus got into a boat with His disciples and said to them, "Let us go across to the other side of the lake."</b>

46:13.260 --> 46:17.530
<b>And as they were sailing, He fell asleep.</b>

46:55.800 --> 46:57.170
<b>Master!</b>

46:57.510 --> 46:59.460
<b>Master!</b>

46:59.840 --> 47:01.880
<b>Jesus!</b>

47:02.230 --> 47:05.380
<b>We are about to die!</b>

47:05.730 --> 47:10.070
<b>The waves are swamping us. We'll all drown! Save us Master!</b>

47:31.760 --> 47:33.630
<b>We're going to be saved!</b>

47:40.550 --> 47:43.050
<b>Where is your faith?</b>

47:53.900 --> 47:59.400
<b>And they sailed on over to Gadara, which is across the lake from Galilee.</b>

48:03.960 --> 48:13.170
<b>(Grunting sounds)</b>

48:13.550 --> 48:23.980
<b>(Growling sounds)</b>

48:24.650 --> 48:26.760
<b>Jesus,</b>

48:27.130 --> 48:31.300
<b>Son of the Most High God,</b>

48:31.670 --> 48:34.190
<b>what do You want with me?</b>

48:34.570 --> 48:35.960
<b>I beg You,</b>

48:36.150 --> 48:37.570
<b>don't punish me!</b>

48:37.760 --> 48:40.070
<b>What is your name?</b>

48:47.320 --> 48:49.480
<b>Legion.</b>

48:49.840 --> 48:51.380
<b>Lord, we beg You,</b>

48:51.550 --> 48:52.380
<b>do not</b>

48:52.440 --> 48:55.440
<b>send us into the abyss.</b>

48:55.590 --> 48:57.190
<b>Let us enter</b>

48:57.380 --> 48:59.230
<b>into the herd</b>

48:59.420 --> 49:00.170
<b>of</b>

49:00.280 --> 49:02.510
<b>swine.</b>

49:13.570 --> 49:14.610
<b>Hey!</b>

49:14.980 --> 49:16.030
<b>Come back!</b>

49:16.170 --> 49:17.710
<b>Stop!</b>

49:18.070 --> 49:20.050
<b>Stop!</b>

49:20.590 --> 49:23.760
<b>And the demons went out of the man... and into the pigs.</b>

49:23.820 --> 49:25.050
<b>Come back!</b>

49:32.920 --> 49:35.400
<b>Go away from here!</b>

49:35.980 --> 49:37.670
<b>You, magician!</b>

49:37.730 --> 49:38.730
<b>Leave us!</b>

49:39.070 --> 49:40.900
<b>Go away from this place!</b>

49:41.090 --> 49:42.230
<b>Leave us!</b>

49:42.420 --> 49:44.480
<b>Go away from here!</b>

49:47.530 --> 49:50.400
<b>I'll follow You wherever You go.</b>

49:51.510 --> 49:52.650
<b>Let me</b>

49:52.860 --> 49:54.070
<b>come with You.</b>

49:54.530 --> 49:56.670
<b>Go back home,</b>

49:57.050 --> 49:59.090
<b>and tell what God has done for you.</b>

50:15.570 --> 50:29.210
<b>Jesus and His disciples withdrew by themselves to Bethsaida.</b>

50:29.570 --> 50:56.210
<b>But multitudes learned about it and followed Him.</b>

50:56.570 --> 51:00.050
<b>Late in the afternoon, Peter said:</b>

51:01.010 --> 51:02.150
<b>Master,</b>

51:02.510 --> 51:04.050
<b>send the people away,</b>

51:04.110 --> 51:07.320
<b>so they can go to the villages and farms around here,</b>

51:07.690 --> 51:12.340
<b>and find food and lodging.  There is nothing in this place.</b>

51:23.230 --> 51:25.190
<b>You yourselves give them something to eat.</b>

51:25.260 --> 51:29.070
<b>But all we have are five loaves and two fish.</b>

51:44.030 --> 51:53.090
<b>Blessed are You, O Lord our God, King of the universe, Who brings forth bread from the earth.</b>

51:59.230 --> 52:01.070
<b>It's a miracle.</b>

52:01.460 --> 52:03.070
<b>Unbelievable!</b>

52:55.230 --> 52:57.050
<b>Who do the crowds say I am?</b>

52:57.300 --> 52:59.730
<b>Some say that You are John the Baptist,</b>

53:00.070 --> 53:02.460
<b>others say that You are Elijah,</b>

53:02.840 --> 53:06.070
<b>while others say that one of the prophets of long ago</b>

53:06.440 --> 53:08.380
<b>has come back to life.</b>

53:09.010 --> 53:10.170
<b>What about you?</b>

53:11.050 --> 53:12.730
<b>Who do you say I am?</b>

53:20.550 --> 53:23.090
<b>You are God's Messiah.</b>

53:27.130 --> 53:29.760
<b>You shall tell no man of this.</b>

53:30.090 --> 53:33.190
<b>The Son of Man must suffer much and be rejected.</b>

53:33.570 --> 53:35.230
<b>He will be put to death,</b>

53:37.030 --> 53:40.070
<b>but three days later will be raised to life.</b>

54:21.840 --> 54:23.440
<b>Will any of you come with Me?</b>

54:23.780 --> 54:25.570
<b>I will follow You Master,</b>

54:26.030 --> 54:29.610
<b>but first, let me go and say good-bye to my family.</b>

54:29.690 --> 54:34.030
<b>Anyone who starts to plow and then keeps looking back is of no use for the kingdom of God.</b>

54:34.760 --> 54:38.030
<b>If anyone wants to come with Me, he must forget himself,</b>

54:38.420 --> 54:41.070
<b>take up his cross every day, and follow Me.</b>

54:43.300 --> 54:47.440
<b>For whoever would save his own life will lose it,</b>

54:47.780 --> 54:51.570
<b>and whoever would lose his life for My sake will save it.</b>

54:51.940 --> 54:56.340
<b>What will it profit a man if he gain the whole earth and lose his own soul?</b>

54:56.800 --> 55:00.440
<b>If any man is ashamed of Me and My teachings,</b>

55:00.820 --> 55:04.440
<b>then the Son of Man will be ashamed of him when He comes in His glory,</b>

55:04.670 --> 55:07.360
<b>and the glory of the Father and the holy angels.</b>

55:12.820 --> 55:14.900
<b>I assure you,</b>

55:15.090 --> 55:20.070
<b>there are some here who will not die until they have seen the kingdom of God.</b>

55:45.300 --> 55:55.690
<b>Then Jesus took John and James and Peter with Him, and went up the hill to pray.</b>

56:07.510 --> 56:16.690
<b>While He was praying, His face changed in its appearance, and His clothes became dazzling white.</b>

56:16.940 --> 56:23.760
<b>Suddenly two men were talking with Him.   They were Moses and Elijah, who appeared in heavenly glory.</b>

56:23.960 --> 56:27.300
<b>You will fulfill God's purpose.</b>

56:27.460 --> 56:30.070
<b>You will die in Jerusalem.</b>

56:49.650 --> 56:52.510
<b>As they were leaving, Peter said to Jesus:</b>

56:52.670 --> 56:57.550
<b>Master, how good it is that we are here.</b>

56:57.900 --> 56:59.650
<b>We will make three tents;</b>

56:59.760 --> 57:00.570
<b>one for You,</b>

57:00.670 --> 57:01.400
<b>one for Moses,</b>

57:01.480 --> 57:02.360
<b>and one for Elijah.</b>

57:02.380 --> 57:08.670
<b>As Peter spoke, a cloud came and overshadowed them and the disciples were afraid.</b>

57:08.760 --> 57:16.610
<b>And a voice came from the cloud saying, "This is My Son, the Chosen One.  Listen to Him".</b>

57:41.420 --> 57:42.610
<b>Teacher!</b>

57:42.760 --> 57:44.010
<b>Teacher,</b>

57:44.260 --> 57:46.610
<b>please do something for my son!</b>

57:46.840 --> 57:51.320
<b>Please, please help him,</b>

57:51.550 --> 57:53.920
<b>for he is my only child.</b>

57:54.150 --> 57:57.630
<b>I've begged Your disciples to cast the demon out of him,</b>

57:57.860 --> 57:59.420
<b>but they could not.</b>

58:00.150 --> 58:03.460
<b>O faithless and perverse generation,</b>

58:03.730 --> 58:07.840
<b>how long am I to be with you and bear with you?</b>

58:08.650 --> 58:10.070
<b>Bring your son here.</b>

59:09.050 --> 59:13.010
<b>His face has been healed too!</b>

59:13.360 --> 59:15.030
<b>How wonderful!</b>

59:43.570 --> 59:45.030
<b>Teach us to pray,</b>

59:45.170 --> 59:47.570
<b>just as John taught his disciples.</b>

59:47.630 --> 59:49.840
<b>When you pray, say,</b>

59:50.030 --> 59:52.550
<b>"Our Father in heaven,</b>

59:52.670 --> 59:55.280
<b>Holy be Your name.</b>

59:55.400 --> 59:57.070
<b>Your kingdom come,</b>

59:57.150 --> 59:59.980
<b>Your will be done on earth as it is in heaven.</b>

1:00:00.130 --> 1:00:02.690
<b>Give us day by day our daily bread.</b>

1:00:02.780 --> 1:00:04.800
<b>And forgive us our sins,</b>

1:00:04.900 --> 1:00:08.170
<b>for we also forgive those who sin against us.</b>

1:00:08.280 --> 1:00:10.400
<b>And lead us not into temptation,</b>

1:00:10.570 --> 1:00:13.090
<b>but deliver us from evil."</b>

1:00:20.400 --> 1:00:23.710
<b>Ask, and you will receive;</b>

1:00:23.920 --> 1:00:27.610
<b>seek, and you will find;</b>

1:00:27.820 --> 1:00:31.280
<b>knock, and the door will be opened to you.</b>

1:00:31.440 --> 1:00:34.320
<b>For everyone who asks will receive,</b>

1:00:34.550 --> 1:00:36.960
<b>and he who seeks will find,</b>

1:00:37.110 --> 1:00:41.090
<b>and the door will be opened to anyone who knocks.</b>

1:00:46.360 --> 1:00:47.400
<b>(laughing)</b>

1:00:47.610 --> 1:00:50.960
<b>Would any of you who are fathers give to your son</b>

1:00:51.170 --> 1:00:53.840
<b>a snake when he asks for a fish,</b>

1:00:54.090 --> 1:00:57.340
<b>or a scorpion when he asks for an egg?</b>

1:00:58.070 --> 1:01:02.590
<b>As bad as you are, you know how to give good things to your children.</b>

1:01:03.510 --> 1:01:10.050
<b>How much more, then, will the Heavenly Father give the Holy Spirit to those who ask Him.</b>

1:01:11.550 --> 1:01:13.130
<b>I tell you this,</b>

1:01:13.340 --> 1:01:16.980
<b>take no thought in your life for what you shall eat,</b>

1:01:17.150 --> 1:01:19.760
<b>nor for your body what you shall wear.</b>

1:01:20.070 --> 1:01:25.860
<b>For life is more than food, and the body more than clothing.</b>

1:01:26.230 --> 1:01:28.940
<b>Consider the ravens:</b>

1:01:29.150 --> 1:01:33.230
<b>They neither sow nor reap, have neither storehouse nor barn,</b>

1:01:33.610 --> 1:01:36.230
<b>yet God feeds them.</b>

1:01:36.880 --> 1:01:41.090
<b>Of how much more worth are you than the birds?</b>

1:01:46.230 --> 1:01:48.570
<b>Which of you, by being anxious,</b>

1:01:48.570 --> 1:01:53.360
<b>can add to the length of your life?</b>

1:01:53.510 --> 1:01:55.960
<b>If you cannot do such a small thing,</b>

1:01:56.340 --> 1:01:59.070
<b>why do you worry about the rest?</b>

1:02:00.320 --> 1:02:03.880
<b>Consider the lilies, how they grow.</b>

1:02:04.050 --> 1:02:06.630
<b>They neither toil nor spin,</b>

1:02:07.190 --> 1:02:12.320
<b>yet Solomon in all his glory was not dressed like a single one of them.</b>

1:02:13.170 --> 1:02:14.510
<b>If God</b>

1:02:14.880 --> 1:02:18.860
<b>so clothes the wild grass today which tomorrow is thrown into a fire,</b>

1:02:19.030 --> 1:02:22.340
<b>how much more sure is He to clothe you,</b>

1:02:22.940 --> 1:02:24.800
<b>O you of little faith.</b>

1:02:24.840 --> 1:02:26.610
<b>Make our faith greater.</b>

1:02:26.730 --> 1:02:29.530
<b>If you had faith as big as a mustard seed, you could say</b>

1:02:29.610 --> 1:02:31.050
<b>to this mulberry tree,</b>

1:02:31.130 --> 1:02:36.030
<b>"Pull yourself up by the roots and plant yourself in the sea," and it would obey you.</b>

1:03:11.440 --> 1:03:14.480
<b>Temptations to sin are sure to come,</b>

1:03:14.690 --> 1:03:17.340
<b>but woe to him by whom they come.</b>

1:03:17.670 --> 1:03:22.070
<b>It would be better for him that a stone were tied about his neck and he were cast into the sea,</b>

1:03:22.150 --> 1:03:26.110
<b>than that he should cause one of these little ones to sin.</b>

1:03:28.150 --> 1:03:30.300
<b>What is the kingdom of God like?</b>

1:03:30.400 --> 1:03:31.980
<b>It is like this:</b>

1:03:32.230 --> 1:03:35.760
<b>A man takes a grain of mustard seed and plants it in his field.</b>

1:03:35.920 --> 1:03:38.260
<b>The plant grows and becomes a tree,</b>

1:03:38.610 --> 1:03:41.420
<b>and the birds make their nests in its branches.</b>

1:03:42.670 --> 1:03:44.730
<b>I'm not sure what He's talking about.</b>

1:03:46.480 --> 1:03:52.050
<b>Why do you eat and drink with tax collectors and other sinners?</b>

1:03:54.300 --> 1:03:58.170
<b>People who are well do not need a doctor, but only those who are sick.</b>

1:03:58.710 --> 1:04:01.590
<b>I have not come to call respectable people to repent,</b>

1:04:01.940 --> 1:04:03.590
<b>but sinners.</b>

1:04:08.570 --> 1:04:10.730
<b>Tell us again about the kingdom.</b>

1:04:10.840 --> 1:04:12.150
<b>Is there anything else?</b>

1:04:12.260 --> 1:04:17.150
<b>Do not be afraid, little flock, for your Father is pleased to give you the kingdom.</b>

1:04:17.230 --> 1:04:20.550
<b>Sell all your belongings and give the money to the poor.</b>

1:04:20.630 --> 1:04:26.690
<b>Provide for yourselves purses that don't wear out and save your riches in Heaven, where they will never decrease.</b>

1:04:27.300 --> 1:04:29.420
<b>Because there no thief can get to them,</b>

1:04:29.780 --> 1:04:32.480
<b>and no moth can destroy them.</b>

1:04:34.760 --> 1:04:38.050
<b>For your heart will always be where your riches are.</b>

1:04:52.300 --> 1:04:53.650
<b>Woman,</b>

1:04:53.980 --> 1:04:56.070
<b>you are free from your sickness.</b>

1:05:06.760 --> 1:05:15.030
<b>Look!  Look, she's cured!  It's a miracle!  Look, look, she's cured!  Come and see!</b>

1:05:16.070 --> 1:05:18.670
<b>Pr-pr-pr-praise</b>

1:05:18.900 --> 1:05:23.380
<b>to the Lord!</b>

1:05:23.530 --> 1:05:25.710
<b>Eighteen years!</b>

1:05:25.920 --> 1:05:28.070
<b>God keep you, Rabbi!</b>

1:05:29.110 --> 1:05:32.010
<b>There are six days in which we should work,</b>

1:05:32.210 --> 1:05:34.920
<b>so come on one of those days to be healed,</b>

1:05:34.980 --> 1:05:37.230
<b>but not on the Sabbath.</b>

1:05:38.900 --> 1:05:40.590
<b>You hypocrites!</b>

1:05:40.780 --> 1:05:45.730
<b>Any one of you would untie his ox or his donkey and take it out from the stall to give it water on the Sabbath.</b>

1:05:46.070 --> 1:05:52.130
<b>Now here is this daughter of Abraham whom Satan has kept in bonds these eighteen years.</b>

1:05:52.280 --> 1:05:56.030
<b>Should she not be released on the Sabbath?</b>

1:06:17.690 --> 1:06:23.070
<b>Good Teacher, what must I do to receive eternal life?</b>

1:06:23.460 --> 1:06:25.960
<b>Why do you call Me good?</b>

1:06:26.110 --> 1:06:28.340
<b>No one is good except God alone.</b>

1:06:28.440 --> 1:06:30.130
<b>You know the commandments:</b>

1:06:30.300 --> 1:06:31.840
<b>"Do not commit adultery."</b>

1:06:32.030 --> 1:06:34.980
<b>"Do not commit murder; do not accuse anyone falsely."</b>

1:06:35.170 --> 1:06:37.170
<b>"Respect your mother and your father."</b>

1:06:37.210 --> 1:06:41.090
<b>Ever since I was young, I have obeyed all these commandments.</b>

1:06:41.400 --> 1:06:44.650
<b>There is still one more thing you need to do.</b>

1:06:44.860 --> 1:06:47.360
<b>You must sell all you have and give the money to the poor,</b>

1:06:47.480 --> 1:06:49.460
<b>and you will have riches in heaven.</b>

1:06:49.630 --> 1:06:51.170
<b>Then come and follow Me.</b>

1:06:51.360 --> 1:06:53.130
<b>But we are merchants;</b>

1:06:53.480 --> 1:06:55.070
<b>wealthy.</b>

1:06:56.590 --> 1:07:00.400
<b>How hard it is for a rich person to enter the Kingdom of God.</b>

1:07:00.760 --> 1:07:04.170
<b>It is harder for a rich person to enter the kingdom of God, than for</b>

1:07:04.400 --> 1:07:07.070
<b>a camel to pass through the eye of a needle.</b>

1:07:08.460 --> 1:07:11.070
<b>(greatly astonished, amazed) Who, then, can be saved?</b>

1:07:12.150 --> 1:07:15.280
<b>What is impossible for man is possible for God.</b>

1:07:15.280 --> 1:07:17.230
<b>Exactly when will this come,</b>

1:07:17.320 --> 1:07:19.090
<b>God's kingdom?</b>

1:07:19.530 --> 1:07:23.190
<b>The kingdom of God does not come in such a way as to be seen.</b>

1:07:23.440 --> 1:07:24.900
<b>No one will say,</b>

1:07:25.030 --> 1:07:26.190
<b>"Look,</b>

1:07:26.320 --> 1:07:28.940
<b>there it is," or "Here it is,"</b>

1:07:29.300 --> 1:07:32.030
<b>because the kingdom of God is within you.</b>

1:07:35.480 --> 1:07:39.400
<b>The time will come when you will wish that you could see one of the days of the Son of Man,</b>

1:07:39.730 --> 1:07:42.670
<b>but you will not see it.</b>

1:07:43.210 --> 1:07:50.510
<b>As the lightning flashes across the sky and lights it up from one side to the other, so will the Son of Man be on His day.</b>

1:07:50.880 --> 1:07:56.050
<b>But first He must suffer much and be rejected by the people of this day.</b>

1:08:14.010 --> 1:08:20.270
<b>Blessed are the eyes which see the things that you see!</b>

1:08:20.470 --> 1:08:25.380
<b>For I tell you, many prophets and kings desired to see what you see, and did not see it,</b>

1:08:25.550 --> 1:08:28.760
<b>and to hear what you hear and did not hear it.</b>

1:08:28.890 --> 1:08:30.550
<b>What should we do?</b>

1:08:30.720 --> 1:08:31.980
<b>What do the Scriptures say?</b>

1:08:32.220 --> 1:08:33.690
<b>How do you interpret them?</b>

1:08:34.350 --> 1:08:36.390
<b>Love the Lord your God with</b>

1:08:36.760 --> 1:08:37.850
<b>all your heart,</b>

1:08:38.020 --> 1:08:39.380
<b>with all your soul,</b>

1:08:39.470 --> 1:08:40.770
<b>with all your strength,</b>

1:08:41.010 --> 1:08:42.970
<b>and with all your mind.</b>

1:08:43.180 --> 1:08:45.180
<b>And love your neighbor as you love yourself.</b>

1:08:45.230 --> 1:08:45.970
<b>You are right.</b>

1:08:46.050 --> 1:08:47.710
<b>Do this and you will live.</b>

1:08:48.140 --> 1:08:49.880
<b>Who is my neighbor?</b>

1:08:49.920 --> 1:08:51.180
<b>Not those soldiers.</b>

1:08:51.300 --> 1:08:52.510
<b>What about Caesar?</b>

1:08:53.230 --> 1:08:56.600
<b>There was once a man going down from Jerusalem to Jericho,</b>

1:08:56.800 --> 1:08:58.590
<b>when robbers attacked him,</b>

1:08:58.730 --> 1:09:03.090
<b>stripped him, beat him, leaving him half dead.</b>

1:09:03.440 --> 1:09:10.800
<b>It so happened that a priest came that way. When he saw the man he walked by on the other side.</b>

1:09:11.130 --> 1:09:18.710
<b>In the same way a Levite also came there, went over and looked at the man, and then walked by on the other side.</b>

1:09:18.880 --> 1:09:22.550
<b>But a despised Samaritan who was traveling on that road came across the man.</b>

1:09:22.640 --> 1:09:25.730
<b>And when he saw him his heart was filled with pity.</b>

1:09:26.230 --> 1:09:30.300
<b>He went over to the man, poured oil and wine on his wounds and bandaged them.</b>

1:09:30.340 --> 1:09:34.510
<b>Then he put him on his own animal and took him to an inn, where he took care of him.</b>

1:09:34.600 --> 1:09:39.720
<b>The next day he gave the innkeeper two silver coins, and he told him to care for the man.</b>

1:09:39.850 --> 1:09:45.600
<b>"And when I come back," he said, "I will pay you whatever else you spend on him."</b>

1:09:47.710 --> 1:09:52.730
<b>Which one of these three acted like a neighbor toward the man who was attacked by the robbers?</b>

1:09:53.380 --> 1:09:55.460
<b>The one who was kind to him.</b>

1:09:55.600 --> 1:09:57.730
<b>You, then, do the same.</b>

1:09:57.810 --> 1:09:58.730
<b>Ah!</b>

1:09:59.550 --> 1:10:02.980
<b>Allow the little children to come to Me and do not forbid them,</b>

1:10:03.350 --> 1:10:06.220
<b>for of such is the kingdom of God.</b>

1:10:06.890 --> 1:10:09.440
<b>Truly, I say to you,</b>

1:10:09.730 --> 1:10:16.480
<b>whoever does not receive the kingdom of God like a little child will in no way enter in.</b>

1:10:16.670 --> 1:10:20.300
<b>Whoever welcomes this child in My name welcomes Me,</b>

1:10:20.520 --> 1:10:24.390
<b>and whoever welcomes Me welcomes the One who sent Me.</b>

1:10:24.640 --> 1:10:28.720
<b>For he who is least among you all is the greatest.</b>

1:11:01.510 --> 1:11:04.270
<b>Hey, what's happening? What's going on?</b>

1:11:04.340 --> 1:11:07.020
<b>Jesus of Nazareth is passing by.</b>

1:11:12.760 --> 1:11:14.590
<b>Jesus!</b>

1:11:17.220 --> 1:11:19.270
<b>Jesus!</b>

1:11:20.800 --> 1:11:25.730
<b>Son of David, have mercy on me!</b>

1:11:32.170 --> 1:11:33.960
<b>What do you want Me to do for you?</b>

1:11:34.060 --> 1:11:36.730
<b>I want to see again.</b>

1:11:42.380 --> 1:11:43.670
<b>Then see.</b>

1:11:44.880 --> 1:11:46.760
<b>Your faith has made you well.</b>

1:11:47.170 --> 1:11:49.470
<b>I can see!</b>

1:11:51.630 --> 1:11:53.390
<b>I can see!</b>

1:11:55.470 --> 1:11:57.470
<b>I can see!</b>

1:11:57.510 --> 1:12:10.720
<b>Praise God! Ah!  He can see!  It’s a miracle!  His eyes are healed!  Praise the Lord!  Amazing!  How wonderful!</b>

1:12:12.230 --> 1:12:19.270
<b>As Jesus was on his way to Jerusalem, large crowds met Him everywhere.</b>

1:12:19.300 --> 1:12:26.730
<b>People were asking Him to show them the way to salvation, and to teach them more about the kingdom of God.</b>

1:12:30.970 --> 1:12:32.760
<b>This Man truly is a prophet.</b>

1:12:32.810 --> 1:12:35.210
<b>My Master, save me!</b>

1:12:42.920 --> 1:12:44.980
<b>Oh, Lord, save us, save us!</b>

1:12:45.060 --> 1:12:46.050
<b>Praise the Lord!</b>

1:12:46.230 --> 1:12:48.800
<b>Show us the true way, Lord!</b>

1:12:49.230 --> 1:12:53.730
<b>The people were beginning to accept Him as Lord. In Jericho there was a tax collector named Zaccheus.</b>

1:12:53.800 --> 1:12:58.050
<b>He wanted to see Jesus so much that he climbed a tree to get above the crowd.</b>

1:12:58.050 --> 1:13:00.130
<b>That's the tax collector.</b>

1:13:01.980 --> 1:13:03.930
<b>Hurry down, Zaccheus,</b>

1:13:04.100 --> 1:13:06.270
<b>for I must stay in your house today.</b>

1:13:06.520 --> 1:13:07.640
<b>My house?</b>

1:13:07.680 --> 1:13:09.730
<b>Who'd want to stay in his house?</b>

1:13:11.940 --> 1:13:13.970
<b>How does Zaccheus know Jesus?</b>

1:13:30.100 --> 1:13:31.300
<b>Listen.</b>

1:13:32.170 --> 1:13:33.260
<b>I give</b>

1:13:33.350 --> 1:13:34.850
<b>half of my belongings</b>

1:13:34.960 --> 1:13:36.060
<b>to the poor,</b>

1:13:36.300 --> 1:13:37.420
<b>and if I have</b>

1:13:37.560 --> 1:13:38.810
<b>cheated anyone,</b>

1:13:38.890 --> 1:13:40.050
<b>I will pay him back</b>

1:13:40.130 --> 1:13:41.850
<b>four times as much.</b>

1:14:02.640 --> 1:14:08.670
<b>I don't believe it, a tax collector paying back his taxes!  Impossible!</b>

1:14:13.220 --> 1:14:15.940
<b>Salvation has come to this house today!</b>

1:14:16.100 --> 1:14:19.010
<b>For this man also is a descendant of Abraham!</b>

1:14:19.230 --> 1:14:22.730
<b>The Son of Man came to seek and to save the lost.</b>

1:14:27.760 --> 1:14:29.100
<b>Listen.</b>

1:14:31.170 --> 1:14:33.050
<b>We are going to Jerusalem,</b>

1:14:34.520 --> 1:14:38.020
<b>where everything the prophets wrote about the Son of Man will come true.</b>

1:14:39.480 --> 1:14:42.230
<b>He will be handed over to the Gentiles.</b>

1:14:43.350 --> 1:14:44.670
<b>They will mock Him,</b>

1:14:44.880 --> 1:14:48.090
<b>and treat Him shamefully, and spit upon Him.</b>

1:14:49.050 --> 1:14:51.710
<b>He will be whipped and killed.</b>

1:14:53.310 --> 1:14:55.140
<b>But on the third day,</b>

1:14:55.270 --> 1:14:57.720
<b>He will rise.</b>

1:15:01.300 --> 1:15:06.520
<b>Even though Jesus knew He was going to be killed for the sins of mankind, He resolutely took the road to Jerusalem.</b>

1:15:06.600 --> 1:15:11.300
<b>He sent two of his disciples to bring a donkey. As He rode along, the crowd rejoiced and praised God,</b>

1:15:11.420 --> 1:15:15.010
<b>proclaiming Jesus as King because of all the miracles they had seen.</b>

1:15:49.890 --> 1:15:52.970
<b>Teacher, command Your disciples to be quiet.</b>

1:15:52.980 --> 1:15:54.970
<b>I tell you that if they were to be quiet,</b>

1:15:55.010 --> 1:15:57.730
<b>the stones themselves would begin shouting.</b>

1:16:00.310 --> 1:16:03.730
<b>Peace in heaven and glory in the highest!</b>

1:16:18.220 --> 1:16:24.730
<b>Jesus came closer to Jerusalem.  And when He saw it, He wept over it.</b>

1:16:29.600 --> 1:16:31.570
<b>If only,</b>

1:16:31.750 --> 1:16:36.630
<b>on this your day, you had known the path for peace, but you have failed to see it.</b>

1:16:37.480 --> 1:16:39.640
<b>The days will come when your enemies</b>

1:16:39.790 --> 1:16:44.250
<b>will build ramparts to surround you and hem you in, pressing hard from every side.</b>

1:16:44.420 --> 1:16:46.750
<b>And within these walls they will destroy you...</b>

1:16:47.540 --> 1:16:49.540
<b>...you and your children.</b>

1:16:50.650 --> 1:16:57.020
<b>And they will not leave one stone upon another in you, because you did not recognize the time of your visitation.</b>

1:17:08.250 --> 1:17:16.710
<b>The holy temple in Jerusalem had become a center of commerce rather than a place of worship.</b>

1:18:05.420 --> 1:18:06.730
<b>It is written,</b>

1:18:07.100 --> 1:18:09.170
<b>"My house shall be a house of prayer,"</b>

1:18:09.210 --> 1:18:11.730
<b>but you have turned it into a den of thieves.</b>

1:18:14.860 --> 1:18:16.820
<b>He's heading for my animals!</b>

1:18:16.890 --> 1:18:17.670
<b>Stop Him!</b>

1:18:17.770 --> 1:18:19.710
<b>Stop Him!</b>

1:18:32.260 --> 1:18:35.690
<b>Get the guards! Get the guards!</b>

1:18:35.960 --> 1:18:42.100
<b>Opposition grew among some of the political and religious leaders because the people were proclaiming Jesus as King.</b>

1:18:45.650 --> 1:18:49.210
<b>I understand that many have already hailed Him as king.</b>

1:18:49.360 --> 1:18:50.900
<b>A king?</b>

1:18:51.270 --> 1:18:53.440
<b>A king of beggars, whores, and thieves.</b>

1:18:53.510 --> 1:18:54.960
<b>We've seen His kind before.</b>

1:18:54.980 --> 1:18:58.140
<b>They come, they make their claims, they go, they're forgotten.</b>

1:18:58.180 --> 1:18:59.570
<b>Don't be blind.</b>

1:18:59.680 --> 1:19:02.500
<b>His following is growing by the day.</b>

1:19:02.820 --> 1:19:04.250
<b>The people admire Him.</b>

1:19:04.270 --> 1:19:07.280
<b>...and think He is a king.</b>

1:19:07.610 --> 1:19:14.730
<b>Let me give you a warning. If this man should threaten the peace further, I shall look to you.</b>

1:19:19.480 --> 1:19:21.420
<b>Perhaps he's right.</b>

1:19:22.110 --> 1:19:24.320
<b>It's time we confronted the Galilean.</b>

1:19:24.510 --> 1:19:33.310
<b>Day after day Jesus spoke against many of the scribes and Pharisees, saying they preached the Law,</b>

1:19:33.460 --> 1:19:38.750
<b>but did not follow the law themselves.</b>

1:19:38.860 --> 1:19:43.710
<b>While in the temple, Jesus saw a very poor widow offering two copper coins.</b>

1:19:43.820 --> 1:19:44.710
<b>It's very little.</b>

1:19:44.790 --> 1:19:45.940
<b>Can't she give more?</b>

1:19:46.130 --> 1:19:47.560
<b>I tell you</b>

1:19:47.930 --> 1:19:50.860
<b>that this poor widow put in more than all the others.</b>

1:19:51.710 --> 1:19:55.820
<b>For the others offered their gifts from what they had to spare of their riches.</b>

1:19:55.960 --> 1:20:02.820
<b>But she, poor as she is, put in all that she had to live on.</b>

1:20:03.250 --> 1:20:04.070
<b>Tell us:</b>

1:20:04.460 --> 1:20:06.750
<b>what right do You have to say these things?</b>

1:20:07.110 --> 1:20:08.750
<b>Who gave You such right?</b>

1:20:08.960 --> 1:20:11.350
<b>Now let Me ask you a question.</b>

1:20:11.690 --> 1:20:15.690
<b>Tell Me, did John's right to baptize come from God or from man?</b>

1:20:22.070 --> 1:20:23.710
<b>What shall we say?</b>

1:20:24.460 --> 1:20:26.150
<b>If we were to say, "from God,"</b>

1:20:26.230 --> 1:20:28.210
<b>He will say, "Why, then,</b>

1:20:28.320 --> 1:20:29.710
<b>don't you believe John?"</b>

1:20:29.850 --> 1:20:33.440
<b>But if we say, "from man,"  this whole crowd here will stone us.</b>

1:20:33.670 --> 1:20:36.710
<b>They're all convinced that John was a prophet.</b>

1:20:39.460 --> 1:20:42.090
<b>We don't know where it came from.</b>

1:20:42.390 --> 1:20:46.250
<b>Neither will I tell you then by what right I do these things.</b>

1:21:02.570 --> 1:21:06.010
<b>There was once a man who planted a vineyard,</b>

1:21:06.250 --> 1:21:08.440
<b>rented it out to tenants,</b>

1:21:08.650 --> 1:21:10.750
<b>and then left home for a long time.</b>

1:21:12.460 --> 1:21:15.320
<b>When the time came to gather the grapes,</b>

1:21:15.540 --> 1:21:17.720
<b>he sent a slave to the tenants,</b>

1:21:18.050 --> 1:21:21.260
<b>to receive from them his share of the harvest.</b>

1:21:21.610 --> 1:21:24.730
<b>But the tenants beat the slave and sent him back without a thing.</b>

1:21:25.090 --> 1:21:26.590
<b>So he sent another slave...</b>

1:21:27.170 --> 1:21:32.300
<b>...but the tenants beat him too, treated him shamefully, and sent him back without a thing.</b>

1:21:32.960 --> 1:21:38.850
<b>Then he sent a third slave. But the tenants wounded him too, and threw him out.</b>

1:21:38.930 --> 1:21:45.600
<b>Then the owner of the vineyard said to himself, "What shall I do? I will send my own dear son."</b>

1:21:45.790 --> 1:21:48.790
<b>"Surely they will respect him."</b>

1:21:49.060 --> 1:21:52.420
<b>But when the tenants saw him coming, they said to one another,</b>

1:21:52.680 --> 1:21:54.650
<b>"This is the owner's son.</b>

1:21:54.850 --> 1:21:58.290
<b>Let's kill him and his property will be ours."</b>

1:21:59.090 --> 1:22:00.710
<b>Tell us more, Lord!</b>

1:22:00.980 --> 1:22:03.360
<b>So they threw him out of the vineyard,</b>

1:22:03.530 --> 1:22:06.570
<b>and killed him.</b>

1:22:06.710 --> 1:22:11.010
<b>What, then, will the owner of the vineyard do to those tenants?</b>

1:22:11.220 --> 1:22:15.710
<b>He will come and kill those men and give the vineyard over to other tenants.</b>

1:22:17.400 --> 1:22:20.320
<b>What, then, does this Scripture mean?</b>

1:22:20.540 --> 1:22:23.690
<b>"The stone which the builders rejected as worthless,</b>

1:22:24.050 --> 1:22:27.190
<b>turned out to be the most important of all."</b>

1:22:27.380 --> 1:22:31.630
<b>Everyone who falls on that stone will be broken to pieces.</b>

1:22:31.800 --> 1:22:34.710
<b>And if that stone falls on someone,</b>

1:22:34.890 --> 1:22:37.070
<b>it will crush him to dust.</b>

1:22:37.400 --> 1:22:38.480
<b>Teacher,</b>

1:22:38.540 --> 1:22:41.300
<b>we know that what You say and teach is right.</b>

1:22:41.500 --> 1:22:45.250
<b>We know that You pay no attention to man's status, but You</b>

1:22:45.400 --> 1:22:48.750
<b>teach the truth about God's will for man.</b>

1:22:50.710 --> 1:22:51.730
<b>Tell us,</b>

1:22:51.820 --> 1:22:56.840
<b>is it against our law for us to pay taxes to the Roman emperor or not?</b>

1:22:57.000 --> 1:22:59.250
<b>Careful, Lord, he's trying to trick you.</b>

1:22:59.350 --> 1:23:02.050
<b>Show Me a silver coin.</b>

1:23:08.880 --> 1:23:11.460
<b>Whose face and name are these on it?</b>

1:23:11.650 --> 1:23:13.130
<b>Caesar!</b>

1:23:13.210 --> 1:23:14.960
<b>Then give to Caesar</b>

1:23:15.210 --> 1:23:17.640
<b>the things that are Caesar's,</b>

1:23:17.970 --> 1:23:19.140
<b>and to God</b>

1:23:19.510 --> 1:23:21.010
<b>the things that are God's.</b>

1:23:22.110 --> 1:23:24.710
<b>What's your answer to that?</b>

1:23:27.460 --> 1:23:38.560
<b>Now the festival of unleavened bread drew near, during which the Passover Lamb would be sacrificed..</b>

1:23:38.930 --> 1:23:44.710
<b>And Jesus sent Peter and John ahead to prepare the Passover meal.</b>

1:24:09.360 --> 1:24:15.060
<b>I have wanted so much to eat this Passover meal with you before I suffer.</b>

1:24:15.430 --> 1:24:17.210
<b>For I tell you,</b>

1:24:17.570 --> 1:24:21.750
<b>I will never eat it again until it is given its full meaning in the kingdom of God.</b>

1:24:34.570 --> 1:24:36.610
<b>Blessed are You O Lord, our God,</b>

1:24:36.960 --> 1:24:38.850
<b>King of the universe,</b>

1:24:39.220 --> 1:24:45.790
<b>Who brings forth fruit from the vine.</b>

1:24:46.150 --> 1:24:48.630
<b>Take this and share it among yourselves.</b>

1:24:49.770 --> 1:24:54.710
<b>For I say to you, I will not drink again of the fruit of the vine until the kingdom of God comes.</b>

1:25:08.480 --> 1:25:10.790
<b>Blessed are You, O Lord, our God,</b>

1:25:11.150 --> 1:25:13.060
<b>King of the universe,</b>

1:25:13.390 --> 1:25:16.710
<b>Who brings forth bread from the earth.</b>

1:25:23.400 --> 1:25:26.770
<b>This is My body which is given for you.</b>

1:25:28.210 --> 1:25:30.710
<b>Do this in remembrance of Me.</b>

1:25:37.610 --> 1:25:43.610
<b>This cup is the new testament in My blood, which is shed for you.</b>

1:25:50.320 --> 1:25:54.320
<b>But, behold, the one who is going to betray Me is with Me at the table.</b>

1:25:54.930 --> 1:26:00.270
<b>And truly the Son of Man must die as God has determined, but woe unto that man by whom He is betrayed.</b>

1:26:00.390 --> 1:26:01.280
<b>(sorrowfully) Is it I?</b>

1:26:01.300 --> 1:26:03.030
<b>Ask Him which one He means.</b>

1:26:03.440 --> 1:26:05.230
<b>Lord, who is it?</b>

1:26:05.750 --> 1:26:08.750
<b>I will never leave you!</b>

1:26:20.960 --> 1:26:24.760
<b>The greatest one among you must be like the youngest,</b>

1:26:26.540 --> 1:26:29.310
<b>and the leader must be like the servant.</b>

1:26:30.770 --> 1:26:32.670
<b>For who is greater,</b>

1:26:33.040 --> 1:26:35.540
<b>the one who sits down to eat,</b>

1:26:35.860 --> 1:26:39.040
<b>or the one who serves?</b>

1:26:39.360 --> 1:26:42.260
<b>The one who sits down, of course.</b>

1:26:44.010 --> 1:26:47.650
<b>But I am among you as one who serves.</b>

1:26:50.650 --> 1:26:54.790
<b>You have stayed with Me all through My trials.</b>

1:26:55.690 --> 1:26:59.260
<b>And just as My Father has given Me the right to rule,</b>

1:26:59.600 --> 1:27:02.650
<b>So I will give you the same right.</b>

1:27:03.030 --> 1:27:06.880
<b>You will eat and drink at My table in My kingdom.</b>

1:27:07.860 --> 1:27:11.710
<b>And you will sit on thrones to rule over the twelve tribes of Israel.</b>

1:27:11.770 --> 1:27:13.290
<b>Then there is no traitor.</b>

1:27:13.380 --> 1:27:15.570
<b>Simon, Simon, listen,</b>

1:27:15.940 --> 1:27:18.400
<b>Satan has earnestly begged God,</b>

1:27:18.790 --> 1:27:23.420
<b>and asked to have all of you, to sift you as wheat is sifted, trying your faith.</b>

1:27:23.790 --> 1:27:27.290
<b>But I have prayed for you, Simon, that your faith may not fail.</b>

1:27:27.610 --> 1:27:30.570
<b>And when you have turned back to Me, you must strengthen your brethren.</b>

1:27:30.670 --> 1:27:31.500
<b>Lord,</b>

1:27:31.820 --> 1:27:34.400
<b>I am ready to go to prison with You,</b>

1:27:34.460 --> 1:27:35.710
<b>and to die with You.</b>

1:27:35.760 --> 1:27:37.000
<b>I tell you, Peter,</b>

1:27:37.100 --> 1:27:41.750
<b>the cock will not crow this day before you shall three times deny that you know Me.</b>

1:27:59.930 --> 1:28:03.400
<b>When I sent you out without purse or bag or shoes, did you lack anything?</b>

1:28:03.480 --> 1:28:03.930
<b>No,</b>

1:28:03.940 --> 1:28:04.800
<b>not a thing.</b>

1:28:05.090 --> 1:28:07.760
<b>But now whoever has a purse or bag must take it,</b>

1:28:08.130 --> 1:28:11.130
<b>and whoever has no sword must sell his mantle and buy one.</b>

1:28:11.350 --> 1:28:12.320
<b>For I tell you,</b>

1:28:12.420 --> 1:28:16.140
<b>it is written in the Scriptures, "And He was counted among the transgressors."</b>

1:28:16.250 --> 1:28:19.750
<b>And what was written about Me is coming true.</b>

1:28:21.250 --> 1:28:22.140
<b>Look,</b>

1:28:22.360 --> 1:28:24.750
<b>here are two swords, Lord.</b>

1:28:34.110 --> 1:28:35.470
<b>Enough of this.</b>

1:28:37.230 --> 1:28:44.300
<b>And the council of the elders met to see how they might rid themselves of Jesus.</b>

1:28:44.670 --> 1:28:50.650
<b>Then entered Satan into Judas, surnamed Iscariot, who was one of the twelve.</b>

1:28:50.750 --> 1:28:55.880
<b>He plotted with the elders to trap Jesus.</b>

1:28:56.250 --> 1:29:02.720
<b>Jesus left Jerusalem and went to the Mount of Olives to pray.</b>

1:29:08.760 --> 1:29:11.730
<b>Pray that you may not enter into temptation.</b>

1:29:16.710 --> 1:29:22.260
<b>Judas Iscariot betrayed Jesus for only thirty pieces of silver.</b>

1:29:22.390 --> 1:29:32.760
<b>Jesus knew that the hour of His death for the sins of mankind was fast approaching; and He prayed.</b>

1:29:53.970 --> 1:29:56.040
<b>Father,</b>

1:29:56.400 --> 1:29:59.040
<b>if You are willing,</b>

1:29:59.400 --> 1:30:03.180
<b>remove this cup from Me.</b>

1:30:03.550 --> 1:30:06.550
<b>Nevertheless,</b>

1:30:06.920 --> 1:30:09.750
<b>not My will but Yours be done.</b>

1:30:13.760 --> 1:30:21.060
<b>And an angel from heaven appeared to Him to strengthen Him.</b>

1:30:21.400 --> 1:30:27.210
<b>And His sweat was as though it were great drops of blood falling to the ground.</b>

1:30:59.500 --> 1:31:02.900
<b>Why are you sleeping?</b>

1:31:03.250 --> 1:31:05.400
<b>Get up,</b>

1:31:05.570 --> 1:31:08.750
<b>and pray that you do not fall into temptation.</b>

1:31:31.770 --> 1:31:33.900
<b>Judas,</b>

1:31:41.190 --> 1:31:44.790
<b>is it with a kiss that you betray the Son of Man?</b>

1:31:48.020 --> 1:31:50.850
<b>Lord, shall we strike with the sword?</b>

1:31:56.110 --> 1:31:57.040
<b>Come on, arrest Him.</b>

1:31:57.070 --> 1:31:58.690
<b>Enough of this!</b>

1:32:08.340 --> 1:32:09.710
<b>A miracle!</b>

1:32:12.770 --> 1:32:16.480
<b>Did you have to come with swords and clubs as though I were an outlaw?</b>

1:32:16.610 --> 1:32:20.680
<b>I was with you every day in the temple and you did not try to arrest Me.</b>

1:32:20.810 --> 1:32:23.690
<b>But this is your hour to act,</b>

1:32:23.850 --> 1:32:26.720
<b>when the power of darkness rules.</b>

1:32:35.400 --> 1:32:36.710
<b>Arrest Him!</b>

1:32:57.130 --> 1:32:58.720
<b>Guard Him well.</b>

1:33:03.560 --> 1:33:08.730
<b>The soldiers took Him into the courtyard and mocked Him as King of the Jews.</b>

1:33:09.730 --> 1:33:12.730
<b>Here's a cloak worn by a king.</b>

1:33:15.040 --> 1:33:16.840
<b>Tell us what's going to happen.</b>

1:33:18.110 --> 1:33:24.470
<b>Are You going to save us, Your Majesty?  Are You going to save us?</b>

1:33:25.860 --> 1:33:28.460
<b>This man too was with Jesus.</b>

1:33:28.790 --> 1:33:30.860
<b>Woman, I don't even know Him.</b>

1:33:31.050 --> 1:33:33.690
<b>I saw them together.</b>

1:33:52.440 --> 1:33:56.250
<b>(mocking laughter) Your humble servants. (mocking laughter)</b>

1:33:57.070 --> 1:34:00.720
<b>(mocking laughter) How does it feel to look up to somebody? (mocking laughter)</b>

1:34:04.000 --> 1:34:06.560
<b>You are one of them, too.</b>

1:34:06.800 --> 1:34:08.720
<b>But I am not.</b>

1:34:34.650 --> 1:34:38.010
<b>There is no doubt that this man was with Jesus,</b>

1:34:38.050 --> 1:34:40.000
<b>because he is also a Galilean.</b>

1:34:40.110 --> 1:34:41.470
<b>Go away.</b>

1:34:41.560 --> 1:34:44.590
<b>I don't know what--what you're talking about.</b>

1:34:49.230 --> 1:34:52.860
<b>Jesus turned and looked straight at Peter.</b>

1:34:53.230 --> 1:34:58.570
<b>Then Peter remembered what the Lord had spoken to him:</b>

1:34:58.940 --> 1:35:04.750
<b>"The cock will not crow this day before you shall three times deny that you know Me."</b>

1:35:10.460 --> 1:35:17.460
<b>Oh Lord,</b>

1:35:17.820 --> 1:35:19.360
<b>I said I would stay with you,</b>

1:35:19.730 --> 1:35:21.860
<b>and die for you,</b>

1:35:22.210 --> 1:35:26.710
<b>But now I have turned from You, and denied I knew you.</b>

1:35:27.900 --> 1:35:29.670
<b>Thou,</b>

1:35:30.040 --> 1:35:36.810
<b>Who did forgive our fathers when they rebelled aginst Thy word;</b>

1:35:37.180 --> 1:35:38.790
<b>Thou,</b>

1:35:39.150 --> 1:35:41.480
<b>Who was angry with them,</b>

1:35:41.820 --> 1:35:43.980
<b>Thou did not destroy them.</b>

1:35:45.350 --> 1:35:54.630
<b>Because of Thy love for them and for Thy Covenant's and faithfulness' sake,</b>

1:35:55.000 --> 1:36:00.750
<b>Thou did spare them.</b>

1:36:05.600 --> 1:36:07.180
<b>Who hit You? Guess.</b>

1:36:07.210 --> 1:36:08.170
<b>Prophesy!</b>

1:36:08.380 --> 1:36:09.750
<b>Who will hit You next?</b>

1:36:11.710 --> 1:36:13.210
<b>Stop it!</b>

1:36:13.570 --> 1:36:15.050
<b>Stop it, I said!</b>

1:36:15.320 --> 1:36:16.750
<b>Bring Him before the council.</b>

1:36:17.810 --> 1:36:19.010
<b>Go!</b>

1:36:25.560 --> 1:36:32.730
<b>The religious council of elders met to question Jesus.</b>

1:36:44.960 --> 1:36:46.250
<b>Tell us,</b>

1:36:46.540 --> 1:36:49.750
<b>are You the Messiah?</b>

1:36:50.150 --> 1:36:51.750
<b>If I tell you,</b>

1:36:52.110 --> 1:36:55.460
<b>you will not believe Me.</b>

1:36:55.790 --> 1:36:59.690
<b>And if I ask you a question, you will not answer Me.</b>

1:37:07.750 --> 1:37:12.710
<b>But from now on the Son of Man will be seated at the right side of Almighty God.</b>

1:37:14.440 --> 1:37:16.180
<b>Are You, then,</b>

1:37:16.510 --> 1:37:18.710
<b>the Son of God?</b>

1:37:19.010 --> 1:37:20.720
<b>You say that I Am.</b>

1:37:24.460 --> 1:37:28.720
<b>Who gives Him the authority to say that?</b>

1:37:29.570 --> 1:37:30.730
<b>Guilty!</b>

1:37:34.400 --> 1:37:37.730
<b>We ourselves have heard what He said.</b>

1:37:42.640 --> 1:37:44.040
<b>We will take Him to Pilate.</b>

1:37:45.710 --> 1:37:49.070
<b>Yes, yes, away with Him!</b>

1:37:56.070 --> 1:37:56.750
<b>Move!</b>

1:38:17.710 --> 1:38:22.090
<b>And they took Him to Pontius Pilate, the most vicious of all Roman governors.</b>

1:38:22.150 --> 1:38:25.360
<b>Pilate himself had sentenced thousands of people to a slow death by nailing them to wooden crosses.</b>

1:38:25.470 --> 1:38:28.810
<b>And what do you want here, at this hour of the morning?</b>

1:38:28.820 --> 1:38:31.290
<b>We caught this Man misleading our people.</b>

1:38:31.320 --> 1:38:34.360
<b>He caused an uproar in the temple market.</b>

1:38:34.430 --> 1:38:35.940
<b>What will be His punishment?</b>

1:38:35.970 --> 1:38:36.790
<b>Sentence Him!</b>

1:38:36.790 --> 1:38:39.720
<b>I see no reason to condemn this Man, no reason.</b>

1:38:39.770 --> 1:38:46.040
<b>We found Him guilty, telling them not to pay taxes to the emperor, claiming Himself the Messiah,</b>

1:38:46.150 --> 1:38:47.180
<b>a king.</b>

1:38:47.310 --> 1:38:49.310
<b>A king?</b>

1:38:50.090 --> 1:38:52.770
<b>Are You the King of the Jews?</b>

1:38:53.270 --> 1:38:54.790
<b>So you say.</b>

1:38:56.690 --> 1:39:00.980
<b>He began teaching in Galilee and now He has come here.</b>

1:39:02.210 --> 1:39:04.780
<b>In Galilee?</b>

1:39:04.880 --> 1:39:08.520
<b>Is this Man a Galilean?</b>

1:39:08.680 --> 1:39:10.320
<b>In that case,</b>

1:39:10.500 --> 1:39:12.820
<b>we'll let Herod deal with Him.</b>

1:39:13.040 --> 1:39:15.930
<b>He's still here in Jerusalem, isn't he?</b>

1:39:16.010 --> 1:39:17.730
<b>Take Him to Herod!</b>

1:39:40.320 --> 1:39:44.390
<b>Who is it that You say You are?</b>

1:39:47.610 --> 1:39:50.770
<b>Who are those You call Your disciples?</b>

1:39:55.100 --> 1:39:59.600
<b>It is said by many You can perform miracles.</b>

1:40:05.070 --> 1:40:07.750
<b>Do one for me.</b>

1:40:08.250 --> 1:40:09.780
<b>My lord,</b>

1:40:10.010 --> 1:40:12.550
<b>He has been corrupting all the people.</b>

1:40:12.760 --> 1:40:14.760
<b>He calls Himself</b>

1:40:15.000 --> 1:40:16.250
<b>the King.</b>

1:40:16.420 --> 1:40:17.820
<b>(ridiculing, mocking) This Man?</b>

1:40:17.930 --> 1:40:22.760
<b>A king? (scoffing laugh)</b>

1:40:28.360 --> 1:40:30.650
<b>Your Majesty.</b>

1:40:32.860 --> 1:40:34.790
<b>Strike Him well.</b>

1:40:40.070 --> 1:40:41.770
<b>Send Him back to Pilate.</b>

1:40:41.850 --> 1:40:43.720
<b>This is his province.</b>

1:41:28.020 --> 1:41:29.060
<b>This Man</b>

1:41:29.210 --> 1:41:32.980
<b>has done nothing to deserve death.</b>

1:41:39.820 --> 1:41:42.210
<b>So I will have Him whipped,</b>

1:41:42.460 --> 1:41:43.790
<b>and let Him go.</b>

1:41:43.900 --> 1:41:48.650
<b>You are obliged to release one man to us at this festival.</b>

1:41:48.690 --> 1:41:49.980
<b>Release to us</b>

1:41:50.350 --> 1:41:51.130
<b>Barabbas.</b>

1:41:51.140 --> 1:41:51.540
<b>Yes.</b>

1:41:51.560 --> 1:41:52.380
<b>Barabbas.</b>

1:41:52.390 --> 1:41:54.100
<b>And away with this Man.</b>

1:41:55.690 --> 1:41:58.690
<b>Yes. Give us Barabbas.</b>

1:42:02.930 --> 1:42:04.510
<b>Crucify Him!</b>

1:42:04.520 --> 1:42:07.000
<b>Yes, crucify Him!</b>

1:42:08.100 --> 1:42:10.510
<b>You, you, whip Him.</b>

1:42:21.420 --> 1:42:23.720
<b>What are you waiting for, Pilate?</b>

1:42:29.720 --> 1:42:30.890
<b>He's Jesus!</b>

1:42:35.760 --> 1:42:38.730
<b>Why do you torment Him so?</b>

1:42:42.000 --> 1:42:44.750
<b>Leave Him, He is the Messiah!</b>

1:42:49.510 --> 1:42:52.750
<b>He has done nothing wrong!</b>

1:43:06.530 --> 1:43:07.760
<b>Lift Him up!</b>

1:43:09.260 --> 1:43:17.640
<b>But they kept on shouting at the top of their voices that Jesus should be crucified.</b>

1:43:18.010 --> 1:43:24.750
<b>So pilate passed the sentence of death on Jesus.  He set free Barabbas, the man they wanted,</b>

1:43:24.790 --> 1:43:32.270
<b>who had been put in prison for riot and murder, and he handed Jesus over to them to be crucified.</b>

1:43:34.520 --> 1:43:35.300
<b>Back!</b>

1:43:35.320 --> 1:43:36.190
<b>Get back!</b>

1:43:36.560 --> 1:43:38.260
<b>Back!  Get back!</b>

1:43:38.630 --> 1:43:39.590
<b>Get away!</b>

1:43:42.460 --> 1:43:44.770
<b>Keep away from Him.</b>

1:43:46.540 --> 1:43:47.670
<b>Get back!</b>

1:43:48.000 --> 1:43:48.770
<b>Get back!</b>

1:43:49.100 --> 1:43:49.770
<b>Back!</b>

1:43:50.290 --> 1:43:51.520
<b>Get away!</b>

1:43:52.440 --> 1:43:53.820
<b>Make room!</b>

1:43:56.140 --> 1:43:57.180
<b>Get out!</b>

1:44:00.250 --> 1:44:02.280
<b>You, out of the way.</b>

1:44:03.570 --> 1:44:06.500
<b>Move when I tell You!</b>

1:44:06.610 --> 1:44:08.390
<b>Get up!</b>

1:44:08.760 --> 1:44:09.880
<b>Get up!</b>

1:44:15.760 --> 1:44:16.770
<b>You!</b>

1:44:17.770 --> 1:44:18.720
<b>What's your name?</b>

1:44:18.770 --> 1:44:20.750
<b>Simon of Cyrene, sir.</b>

1:44:20.750 --> 1:44:22.050
<b>Step over here!</b>

1:44:23.600 --> 1:44:24.860
<b>Cut the ropes!</b>

1:44:30.400 --> 1:44:32.610
<b>You, carry it.</b>

1:44:32.960 --> 1:44:36.820
<b>Come on, move!</b>

1:44:37.190 --> 1:44:40.960
<b>Back!</b>

1:44:41.320 --> 1:44:43.930
<b>Back,</b>

1:44:44.260 --> 1:44:51.230
<b>Leave Him!</b>

1:44:51.600 --> 1:44:55.040
<b>Move on, clear the way there.</b>

1:45:12.250 --> 1:45:12.690
<b>Back,</b>

1:45:13.050 --> 1:45:14.600
<b>Get back!</b>

1:45:19.060 --> 1:45:21.670
<b>Get back!</b>

1:45:29.860 --> 1:45:34.390
<b>We weep for You, Lord, we weep. Drink this, drink.</b>

1:45:34.460 --> 1:45:36.710
<b>Drink, Lord.</b>

1:45:40.980 --> 1:45:43.020
<b>Women of Jerusalem,</b>

1:45:43.380 --> 1:45:45.500
<b>don't weep for Me,</b>

1:45:45.820 --> 1:45:50.320
<b>but weep for yourselves and for your children.</b>

1:45:50.690 --> 1:45:54.730
<b>For if such things as these take place when the wood is green,</b>

1:45:55.100 --> 1:45:57.730
<b>what will happen when it is dry?</b>

1:45:58.860 --> 1:45:59.930
<b>God help You.</b>

1:46:01.030 --> 1:46:03.060
<b>We will pray for You.</b>

1:46:08.400 --> 1:46:10.010
<b>Move!</b>

1:46:10.340 --> 1:46:11.210
<b>Down here!</b>

1:46:11.270 --> 1:46:11.750
<b>Come on!</b>

1:46:11.900 --> 1:46:13.010
<b>Quicker,</b>

1:46:13.350 --> 1:46:14.820
<b>quicker.</b>

1:46:15.180 --> 1:46:17.150
<b>Now you, go!</b>

1:46:17.520 --> 1:46:20.110
<b>Go on, keep up, quicker, come on!</b>

1:46:20.460 --> 1:46:21.720
<b>Quicker!</b>

1:46:22.060 --> 1:46:23.360
<b>Now move!</b>

1:46:23.720 --> 1:46:24.790
<b>Move!</b>

1:46:25.150 --> 1:46:26.540
<b>Now, You go ahead!</b>

1:46:26.860 --> 1:46:28.760
<b>Come on now.</b>

1:47:31.560 --> 1:47:34.610
<b>Get on with it.</b>

1:48:03.780 --> 1:48:06.340
<b>Raise the cross!</b>

1:48:22.040 --> 1:48:24.310
<b>You, put the peg in!</b>

1:48:29.820 --> 1:48:32.180
<b>Support ropes loose!</b>

1:48:52.040 --> 1:48:54.400
<b>Forgive them, Father,</b>

1:48:55.570 --> 1:48:57.710
<b>for they don't know what they're doing.</b>

1:49:13.320 --> 1:49:14.800
<b>He has saved others;</b>

1:49:15.150 --> 1:49:17.730
<b>let Him save Himself.</b>

1:49:18.630 --> 1:49:24.750
<b>Yes, save Yourself if You're the Messiah! Come down from the cross.</b>

1:49:25.070 --> 1:49:27.750
<b>Show us one of Your miracles!</b>

1:49:53.270 --> 1:49:57.250
<b>And Jesus was crucified between two thieves in fulfillment of prophesy,</b>

1:49:57.320 --> 1:50:01.280
<b>as the prophets of God had predicted hundreds of years before.</b>

1:50:06.900 --> 1:50:10.250
<b>This is no ordinary mystic's garment.</b>

1:50:10.300 --> 1:50:11.860
<b>(Laughter)</b>

1:50:11.920 --> 1:50:16.650
<b>Here! Let go! No, don't tear it! I'll tell you what:</b>

1:50:16.790 --> 1:50:18.190
<b>let's play for this!</b>

1:50:27.300 --> 1:50:31.770
<b>Ah, you're so lucky! What will you do with it now that you've won it?</b>

1:50:42.250 --> 1:50:51.230
<b>And a sign was placed above His head that read, "This is the King of the Jews."</b>

1:51:07.880 --> 1:51:11.750
<b>Save Yourself if You are the King of the Jews.</b>

1:52:09.270 --> 1:52:10.670
<b>Aren't</b>

1:52:11.040 --> 1:52:12.360
<b>You</b>

1:52:12.710 --> 1:52:16.900
<b>the Messiah?</b>

1:52:17.290 --> 1:52:19.380
<b>Save</b>

1:52:19.710 --> 1:52:22.480
<b>Yourself,</b>

1:52:22.820 --> 1:52:26.150
<b>and--and us.</b>

1:52:26.460 --> 1:52:28.420
<b>Don't you fear God?</b>

1:52:28.790 --> 1:52:31.500
<b>We received the same sentence</b>

1:52:31.860 --> 1:52:33.260
<b>He did,</b>

1:52:33.630 --> 1:52:36.860
<b>but He has done no wrong.</b>

1:52:42.800 --> 1:52:44.510
<b>Remember me, Jesus,</b>

1:52:44.840 --> 1:52:47.750
<b>when You--when You come as King.</b>

1:52:49.180 --> 1:52:52.510
<b>I promise you,</b>

1:52:52.850 --> 1:52:55.820
<b>today you will be in Paradise</b>

1:52:56.180 --> 1:52:57.750
<b>with Me.</b>

1:53:04.320 --> 1:53:11.770
<b>It was now noon and a darkness fell across the whole land for three hours, until 3 o'clock.</b>

1:53:38.960 --> 1:53:42.730
<b>The curtain of the temple was torn right down the middle.</b>

1:54:00.850 --> 1:54:02.840
<b>Father,</b>

1:54:06.390 --> 1:54:09.390
<b>into Your hands</b>

1:54:09.720 --> 1:54:12.590
<b>I commit</b>

1:54:12.960 --> 1:54:18.730
<b>My Spirit.</b>

1:54:22.270 --> 1:54:27.020
<b>Now when the captain of the soldiers saw what had happened, he glorified God, saying:</b>

1:54:27.750 --> 1:54:34.750
<b>Glory be to God! Certainly this was a righteous Man.</b>

1:54:40.050 --> 1:54:45.460
<b>Joseph of Arimathea, a righteous member of the religious council who had not consented to this deed,</b>

1:54:45.540 --> 1:54:53.790
<b>obtained permission from Pontius Pilate to lay Jesus' body in a tomb before the worship day began at sundown.</b>

1:56:01.530 --> 1:56:05.430
<b>We'll get spices and ointments to prepare the body of our Lord.</b>

1:56:05.430 --> 1:56:07.140
<b>I will help.</b>

1:56:07.510 --> 1:56:08.320
<b>But hurry,</b>

1:56:08.380 --> 1:56:10.750
<b>the Sabbath is approaching.</b>

1:56:35.100 --> 1:56:43.090
<b>They went back home and prepared the spices for the body. On the sabbath day they rested as commanded by the Law.</b>

1:56:43.110 --> 1:56:50.770
<b>Very early on Sunday morning, they came to the tomb carrying the spices they had prepared.</b>

1:56:52.250 --> 1:57:00.760
<b>They found the stone rolled away from the tomb. But when they entered, the body of the Lord Jesus was gone.</b>

1:57:26.750 --> 1:57:33.010
<b>Why do you seek the living among the dead? He is not here, but is risen.</b>

1:57:33.090 --> 1:57:36.100
<b>Remember what He said to you while He was in Galilee:</b>

1:57:36.210 --> 1:57:44.790
<b>"The Son of Man will be handed over to sinful men, be crucified, and on the third day rise again."</b>

1:57:57.750 --> 1:57:58.770
<b>Listen!</b>

1:57:59.110 --> 1:58:01.110
<b>The stone was rolled away!</b>

1:58:01.500 --> 1:58:02.960
<b>We entered,</b>

1:58:03.320 --> 1:58:06.730
<b>and the body of our Lord was</b>

1:58:06.920 --> 1:58:07.690
<b>gone.</b>

1:58:07.760 --> 1:58:09.820
<b>What? The body of our Lord, gone?</b>

1:58:09.820 --> 1:58:11.630
<b>And two men appeared to us;</b>

1:58:12.000 --> 1:58:13.540
<b>angels, shining,</b>

1:58:13.900 --> 1:58:15.250
<b>like the sun.</b>

1:58:15.600 --> 1:58:17.770
<b>And said to us:</b>

1:58:18.140 --> 1:58:20.140
<b>"Why do you look for the living</b>

1:58:20.510 --> 1:58:22.180
<b>among the dead?"</b>

1:58:22.540 --> 1:58:24.750
<b>It's true.</b>

1:58:26.460 --> 1:58:28.550
<b>Believe us.</b>

1:58:28.880 --> 1:58:29.880
<b>Believe us.</b>

1:58:29.920 --> 1:58:36.760
<b>We saw them! Go and see for yourself!  The tomb was empty! Our Lord was gone!</b>

1:58:37.090 --> 1:58:39.760
<b>Peter, you must believe us!</b>

1:59:15.260 --> 1:59:20.730
<b>Jesus appeared to two of the disciples. They excitedly came back to the others.</b>

1:59:20.860 --> 1:59:22.900
<b>The Lord is risen indeed!</b>

1:59:23.250 --> 1:59:24.750
<b>He has appeared to Simon!</b>

1:59:24.880 --> 1:59:27.440
<b>We didn't recognize Him;</b>

1:59:27.810 --> 1:59:28.750
<b>not on the road.</b>

1:59:28.790 --> 1:59:29.820
<b>But when He broke bread,</b>

1:59:29.940 --> 1:59:30.920
<b>then we knew Him.</b>

1:59:30.930 --> 1:59:31.750
<b>At Emmaus.</b>

1:59:31.860 --> 1:59:33.750
<b>How strange He should go there.</b>

1:59:43.760 --> 1:59:45.760
<b>Peace be with you.</b>

1:59:56.770 --> 1:59:59.770
<b>Why are you troubled?</b>

2:00:00.140 --> 2:00:03.840
<b>Why are these doubts coming up in your minds?</b>

2:00:04.180 --> 2:00:05.050
<b>Look</b>

2:00:05.400 --> 2:00:07.550
<b>at My hands and My feet,</b>

2:00:07.900 --> 2:00:10.350
<b>and see that it is I Myself.</b>

2:00:10.680 --> 2:00:13.250
<b>Feel Me and you will know.</b>

2:00:14.920 --> 2:00:18.760
<b>For a spirit has not flesh and bones as you see I have.</b>

2:00:19.090 --> 2:00:22.390
<b>These are the very things I spoke to you about while I was still with you,</b>

2:00:23.250 --> 2:00:25.480
<b>...that everything written about Me in the Law of Moses</b>

2:00:25.540 --> 2:00:30.110
<b>and the writings of the prophets and the Psalms had to come true.</b>

2:00:30.320 --> 2:00:32.470
<b>This is what is written:</b>

2:00:32.650 --> 2:00:34.570
<b>the Messiah must suffer,</b>

2:00:34.750 --> 2:00:37.010
<b>and rise from the dead on the third day,</b>

2:00:37.460 --> 2:00:38.880
<b>...and in His name</b>

2:00:39.250 --> 2:00:43.920
<b>the message of repentance and the forgiveness of sins must be preached to all nations,</b>

2:00:44.290 --> 2:00:46.420
<b>beginning in Jerusalem.</b>

2:00:47.290 --> 2:00:49.820
<b>You are witnesses of these things.</b>

2:00:50.040 --> 2:00:53.340
<b>I Myself will send you the One My Father has promised.</b>

2:00:53.460 --> 2:00:55.130
<b>But you must wait in the city</b>

2:00:55.500 --> 2:00:58.730
<b>until the power from above comes down upon you.</b>

2:01:27.590 --> 2:01:31.400
<b>The Lord bless you and keep you.</b>

2:01:31.770 --> 2:01:35.400
<b>All power is given to Me in heaven and in earth.</b>

2:01:35.570 --> 2:01:45.320
<b>Go, then, and teach all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit,</b>

2:01:45.430 --> 2:01:50.930
<b>teaching them to observe all things I have commanded you.</b>

2:01:51.060 --> 2:01:59.500
<b>And surely I am with you always, even unto the end of the world.</b>

2:02:16.800 --> 2:02:22.850
<b>In The Holy Scriptures, God declared the Messiah would come to be the Savior of the world.</b>

2:02:22.930 --> 2:02:29.750
<b>The life of Jesus gives evidence that He is indeed the One the prophets spoke about.</b>

2:02:29.790 --> 2:02:35.850
<b>Isaiah prophesied that, The virgin will conceive a child and will give birth to a son.</b>

2:02:35.930 --> 2:02:43.640
<b>Centuries later, the birth of Jesus was the fulfillment of that prophecy.</b>

2:02:43.820 --> 2:02:49.630
<b>The Holy Scriptures declared that the Holy One to be born would be called the Son of God.</b>

2:02:49.680 --> 2:02:56.460
<b>This means that Jesus was to be called the Son of God.</b>

2:02:56.520 --> 2:02:59.960
<b>And we see this in how he lived His life.</b>

2:03:00.020 --> 2:03:04.020
<b>He Healed people from disease, forgave their sins,</b>

2:03:04.100 --> 2:03:10.350
<b>turned them back to God and promised them a place in God's eternal kingdom.</b>

2:03:10.510 --> 2:03:19.550
<b>He offered Himself as a sacrifice for sin in their place and then rose again, conquering death.</b>

2:03:19.820 --> 2:03:27.960
<b>Jesus said, No one can take my life from me. I lay it down of my own accord.</b>

2:03:28.000 --> 2:03:32.140
<b>The life of Jesus not only fulfilled  the writings of the prophets,</b>

2:03:32.180 --> 2:03:35.710
<b>but also confirmed the truth of God's Holy Word.</b>

2:03:36.320 --> 2:03:43.130
<b>The prophets declared, The Word of the Lord is flawless, Your Word, oh, Lord, is eternal.</b>

2:03:43.180 --> 2:03:52.760
<b>Jesus Himself said, Heaven and earth will pass away, but My words will never pass away.</b>

2:03:52.820 --> 2:04:01.150
<b>Jesus came to give us life in all its fullness. But when man disobeyed God in the Garden of Eden,</b>

2:04:01.220 --> 2:04:08.060
<b>he chose to go his own way, and his actions separated him from the Creator.</b>

2:04:08.390 --> 2:04:15.210
<b>The Holy Scriptures declare that all have sinned and the payment for sin is death,</b>

2:04:15.270 --> 2:04:20.090
<b>this means a spiritual death, eternal separation from God.</b>

2:04:20.220 --> 2:04:24.560
<b>But just as God provided a ram to die in place of Abraham's son,</b>

2:04:24.630 --> 2:04:29.690
<b>so He sent Jesus the Messiah to die in our place.</b>

2:04:29.760 --> 2:04:39.260
<b>His life, death and resurrection restored the relationship between God who put their trust in Him.</b>

2:04:39.300 --> 2:04:47.680
<b>Now, those who follow Jesus not only have their sins forgiven, but are saved from God's eternal judgment.</b>

2:04:47.800 --> 2:04:53.100
<b>They are assured of paradise and will live with Him forever.</b>

2:04:53.150 --> 2:05:00.800
<b>It is this life and freedom from the guilt and power of sin that Jesus offers each person today.</b>

2:05:00.850 --> 2:05:07.250
<b>This does not mean following a religion  but choosing to have  faith in Jesus who says,</b>

2:05:07.250 --> 2:05:09.630
<b>I stand at the door and knock.</b>

2:05:10.060 --> 2:05:16.520
<b>If anyone hears my voice and opens the door, I will come into Him.</b>

2:05:16.600 --> 2:05:23.130
<b>This means turning to God and trusting Jesus to come into our lives, to forgive our sins</b>

2:05:23.190 --> 2:05:26.300
<b>and to make us what He wants us to be.</b>

2:05:26.350 --> 2:05:32.560
<b>It is not enough to intellectually agree with His claims, nor to have an emotional experience.</b>

2:05:32.640 --> 2:05:39.310
<b>We receive Him by grace through faith as an act of the will.</b>

2:05:39.600 --> 2:05:47.770
<b>When people are ready to become followers of Jesus the Messiah, they may speak to Him in a simple prayer.</b>

2:05:48.000 --> 2:05:52.300
<b>Perhaps you are ready now to open your life to God.</b>

2:05:52.350 --> 2:05:58.600
<b>If so, you may join in the following prayer to Him silently in your heart;</b>

2:05:58.650 --> 2:06:04.380
<b>Lord Jesus, I need you.</b>

2:06:04.420 --> 2:06:12.170
<b>Thank you for dying on the cross for my sins.</b>

2:06:12.320 --> 2:06:19.420
<b>I confess and repent of my sins.</b>

2:06:19.720 --> 2:06:30.810
<b>I open the door of my life and  receive You as my Savior and Lord.</b>

2:06:31.090 --> 2:06:42.060
<b>Thank you for forgiving my sins and giving me eternal life.</b>

2:06:42.350 --> 2:06:49.550
<b>Make me the kind of person you want me to be,</b>

2:06:49.820 --> 2:06:55.770
<b>as I become one of your followers.</b>

2:06:56.220 --> 2:06:58.350
<b>Amen.</b>

2:07:00.630 --> 2:07:09.480
<b>Jesus said about His followers, My sheep recognize My voice. I know them, and they follow Me.</b>

2:07:09.780 --> 2:07:14.020
<b>In order to experience the abundant life which Jesus promised,</b>

2:07:14.220 --> 2:07:20.890
<b>His followers talk to God each day in prayer and read or listen to His word.</b>

2:07:20.970 --> 2:07:27.190
<b>They tell others about Him and meet regularly with those  who love and follow Him.</b>

2:07:27.300 --> 2:07:30.110
<b>Remember His wonderful promise.</b>

2:07:30.190 --> 2:07:41.690
<b>All power is given to Me in Heaven and in earth. Low, I am with you always, even to the end of the world.</b>
